WEBVTT

00:00:07.688 --> 00:00:12.300
Moving house.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.412
A cup of tea?

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:15.632
Yes dear.

00:00:15.692 --> 00:00:18.954
Yes dear.

00:00:19.014 --> 00:00:22.406
Yes dear.

00:00:22.466 --> 00:00:24.117
Here you are.

00:00:24.177 --> 00:00:26.828
Yes dear.

00:00:26.888 --> 00:00:30.781
I'll go and open the door for Boris, Josie.

00:00:30.841 --> 00:00:32.522
Why do I have to do it?

00:00:32.542 --> 00:00:37.320
Don't argue, just do it.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.920
Get down Boris!

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.042
Here you are Boris.

00:00:43.102 --> 00:00:44.294
Have my piece of toast.

00:00:44.354 --> 00:00:47.693
Don't feed him at the table, Josie.

00:00:47.753 --> 00:00:52.850
There's another competition in the newspaper I can enter Nancy.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:54.721
What can you win this time?

00:00:54.741 --> 00:00:58.193
A ticket for a Marilyn Manson concert.

00:00:58.253 --> 00:01:00.214
Do you know who that is?

00:01:00.274 --> 00:01:02.125
No, but isn't she a singer?

00:01:02.165 --> 00:01:04.927
A bit like Nanamu Scory.

00:01:04.986 --> 00:01:06.778
Yes, that's right.

00:01:06.838 --> 00:01:07.888
Just like her.

00:01:07.948 --> 00:01:08.969
I hope you win.

00:01:08.989 --> 00:01:11.464
Oh, just ignore him, Mum.

00:01:11.524 --> 00:01:17.974
Nancy, it says here that your day is going to be full of fun and laughter.

00:01:18.034 --> 00:01:19.745
I don't think so.

00:01:19.805 --> 00:01:22.778
Why do you look at the horoscope every day, Mum?

00:01:22.838 --> 00:01:24.130
It's fun.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:27.016
Let me look at Josephine's stars.

00:01:27.076 --> 00:01:28.922
Oh, yes, here it is.

00:01:28.982 --> 00:01:34.673
It says that you're feeling off colour today, and it's better to stay indoors.

00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:36.674
Yeah, you're right, Gran.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.654
I have a stomach ache.

00:01:38.714 --> 00:01:40.644
I'm not going to school today.

00:01:40.704 --> 00:01:42.135
Stop that, Josephine.

00:01:42.195 --> 00:01:43.635
You are going to school?

00:01:43.695 --> 00:01:44.485
No arguments.

00:01:44.525 --> 00:01:46.395
Oh, why do I have to go to school?

00:01:46.455 --> 00:01:47.486
I hate it!

00:01:47.546 --> 00:01:48.486
It's boring.

00:01:48.506 --> 00:01:49.236
Because you do.

00:01:49.296 --> 00:01:51.006
I hated school, too.

00:01:51.066 --> 00:01:52.806
The teachers were terrible.

00:01:52.866 --> 00:01:55.287
They used to cane us with sticks.

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:57.197
Do they cane you, Grand?

00:01:57.257 --> 00:01:58.638
Yes, of course.

00:01:58.698 --> 00:02:01.089
I was cained by the headmaster.

00:02:01.148 --> 00:02:02.619
What was his name?

00:02:02.679 --> 00:02:04.890
Oh, yes, Mr. Payne.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.940
I put some glue on a seat.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.521
That's not so bad.

00:02:08.581 --> 00:02:09.871
Why did he cane you?

00:02:09.931 --> 00:02:13.012
Because it was the teacher's toilet seat.

00:02:13.052 --> 00:02:13.772
Really?

00:02:13.832 --> 00:02:14.782
Wow.

00:02:14.842 --> 00:02:15.703
Cool.

00:02:15.762 --> 00:02:18.203
Don't get ideas, Josephine.

00:02:18.263 --> 00:02:19.744
Go and get ready for school.

00:02:19.804 --> 00:02:21.834
Oh, Mom, please.

00:02:21.854 --> 00:02:23.515
Do as I tell you.

00:02:23.535 --> 00:02:25.199
Now.

00:02:25.258 --> 00:02:28.812
Teenagers.

00:02:28.872 --> 00:02:32.483
And put that newspaper down, Pete.

00:02:32.543 --> 00:02:33.003
Sorry?

00:02:33.023 --> 00:02:34.494
Is there a problem?

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.574
No, no.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:41.225
I was just trying to get our daughter to go to school.

00:02:41.285 --> 00:02:43.455
Thank you for helping me.

00:02:43.515 --> 00:02:45.096
It's OK, dear.

00:02:45.156 --> 00:02:46.786
I'm always happy to help.

00:02:46.846 --> 00:02:48.626
Can you pass the toast, please?

00:02:48.686 --> 00:02:50.377
Didn't you hear what I said?

00:02:50.437 --> 00:02:51.827
Yes, dear, of course, dear.

00:02:51.887 --> 00:02:53.607
And the tree core, please.

00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:54.548
Here it is.

00:02:54.568 --> 00:02:55.829
Ow!

00:02:55.889 --> 00:02:58.101
Why did you do that?

00:02:58.161 --> 00:03:00.322
Look, it's all over my trousers.

00:03:00.382 --> 00:03:01.782
I don't believe it.

00:03:01.842 --> 00:03:03.484
Get down, Boris!

00:03:03.544 --> 00:03:04.554
I'm not playing.

00:03:04.614 --> 00:03:06.195
Do something!

00:03:06.255 --> 00:03:09.387
Go to work now, Pete, before I do something else to you.

00:03:09.447 --> 00:03:13.440
The next time it might be a kitchen knife, so be careful in future.

00:03:13.499 --> 00:03:14.540
What's the matter?

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:15.640
What did I do?

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.172
Nothing, Pete.

00:03:17.232 --> 00:03:18.992
Absolutely nothing.

00:03:19.052 --> 00:03:21.044
That's the problem.

00:03:21.104 --> 00:03:22.454
I'm going.

00:03:22.514 --> 00:03:27.064
Goodbye.

00:03:27.124 --> 00:03:32.835
Why did you marry him, Nancy?

00:03:32.895 --> 00:03:34.536
Do you want someone new as well?

00:03:34.596 --> 00:03:37.388
I always said he was bone idle.

00:03:37.448 --> 00:03:40.209
I liked that lawyer you went out with once.

00:03:40.269 --> 00:03:42.480
Nice eyes and a lovely smile.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:45.842
I don't want to hear what you think, Mum.

00:03:45.902 --> 00:03:48.123
Ooh!

00:03:48.183 --> 00:03:50.494
It's not a good day for Pete.

00:03:50.554 --> 00:03:54.646
It says in his horoscope that he gets some bad news this afternoon.

00:03:54.706 --> 00:03:55.647
Stop it, Mum.

00:03:55.707 --> 00:03:57.078
Don't make things worse.

00:03:57.138 --> 00:04:01.690
I must tell Pete, he must be careful.

00:04:01.749 --> 00:04:05.140
Nancy?

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.572
Yes?

00:04:06.632 --> 00:04:08.604
What do you want now?

00:04:08.664 --> 00:04:11.341
I can't find any clean trousers.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:15.177
They're in the fridge between the cheese and the tomatoes.

00:04:15.237 --> 00:04:17.539
Why are they in the fridge?

00:04:17.599 --> 00:04:19.050
Where do you think they are?

00:04:19.109 --> 00:04:20.341
In the bedroom.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.272
Left wardrobe on the right where they always are.

00:04:23.332 --> 00:04:24.333
Thank you Nancy.

00:04:24.393 --> 00:04:25.274
Pete?

00:04:25.333 --> 00:04:26.664
Yes, what do you want?

00:04:26.724 --> 00:04:28.115
Be careful.

00:04:28.175 --> 00:04:30.627
Today is a bad day for you.

00:04:30.687 --> 00:04:31.247
Sorry?

00:04:31.307 --> 00:04:35.050
It says in your horoscope that you get some bad news.

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:36.971
Not that rubbish again.

00:04:37.031 --> 00:04:38.802
I'm not interested.

00:04:38.862 --> 00:04:40.422
Wait a minute.

00:04:40.482 --> 00:04:43.011
Do you believe all that rubbish in the horoscope?

00:04:43.071 --> 00:04:44.772
Sometimes it's true, you know.

00:04:44.832 --> 00:04:47.164
Well, you're the same star sign as me.

00:04:47.224 --> 00:04:48.645
So you be careful.

00:04:48.705 --> 00:04:50.746
Oh dear, I forgot.

00:04:50.806 --> 00:04:52.917
Maybe you fall down the stairs.

00:04:52.977 --> 00:04:54.979
Maybe Boris bites your leg.

00:04:55.039 --> 00:04:57.090
Maybe your hearing aid explodes.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.220
Maybe.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:04.016
Goodbye.

00:05:04.076 --> 00:05:11.061
I told you not to say anything.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.931
Now, where is Josephine?

00:05:12.951 --> 00:05:14.492
She's going to be late.

00:05:14.552 --> 00:05:17.603
Can you go upstairs and tell us a hurry up, please, Mum?

00:05:17.663 --> 00:05:19.944
I have to make her sandwiches.

00:05:20.004 --> 00:05:22.504
Oh, what a family.

00:05:22.564 --> 00:05:24.055
OK, Nancy.

00:05:24.115 --> 00:05:25.655
Come on, Boris.

00:05:25.715 --> 00:05:27.156
There's a good dog.

00:05:27.216 --> 00:05:35.216
You don't want to bite my lad, do you?

00:05:35.276 --> 00:05:42.656
Oh, there you are, Josie.

00:05:42.716 --> 00:05:44.778
Come on, your mother is waiting.

00:05:44.838 --> 00:05:47.550
Josh, close the door, Grand.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.802
Can you keep a secret?

00:05:49.862 --> 00:05:52.134
Oh, I love secrets.

00:05:52.194 --> 00:05:53.685
Come here.

00:05:53.745 --> 00:05:55.366
Look here.

00:05:55.426 --> 00:05:57.718
In this box.

00:05:57.778 --> 00:06:01.592
Oh, it's Robbie the Rat.

00:06:01.652 --> 00:06:02.572
I thought...

00:06:02.632 --> 00:06:03.242
Yes, I know.

00:06:03.302 --> 00:06:04.924
Dad told me to sell him.

00:06:04.984 --> 00:06:06.625
But I want to keep him.

00:06:06.685 --> 00:06:08.972
Oh, he's so sweet.

00:06:09.032 --> 00:06:13.374
Oh, look at his lovely little eyes and funny nose.

00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:17.999
He really looks like your father.

00:06:18.019 --> 00:06:20.402
Don't tell mum or dad he's here in my room.

00:06:20.462 --> 00:06:21.474
Please.

00:06:21.534 --> 00:06:22.695
I promise.

00:06:22.755 --> 00:06:29.145
It's our secret.

00:06:29.205 --> 00:06:36.234
It's nice to put my feet up for a moment.

00:06:36.294 --> 00:06:38.415
You work too hard.

00:06:38.475 --> 00:06:42.426
Pete and Josephine should do more around the house to help you.

00:06:42.486 --> 00:06:43.867
Stop it, Mum.

00:06:43.926 --> 00:06:47.088
Can you pass me another biscuit, please?

00:06:47.148 --> 00:06:52.610
I just want a few minutes of peace and quiet.

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:54.710
Oh, dear.

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:56.781
I wonder who that is.

00:06:56.841 --> 00:06:58.541
Can you answer it, Mum?

00:06:58.601 --> 00:07:00.792
All right.

00:07:00.852 --> 00:07:03.432
Hello?

00:07:03.492 --> 00:07:05.594
Who is it?

00:07:05.653 --> 00:07:08.329
Sorry, Pete!

00:07:08.389 --> 00:07:09.792
Speak up!

00:07:09.852 --> 00:07:11.086
What does he want?

00:07:11.145 --> 00:07:12.386
Sorry?

00:07:12.446 --> 00:07:15.487
Yes, all right.

00:07:15.507 --> 00:07:15.968
Bye.

00:07:16.028 --> 00:07:17.058
Yes?

00:07:17.118 --> 00:07:19.230
He said he's coming home now.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.262
But what did he want?

00:07:21.322 --> 00:07:24.104
Something about he forgot the bag.

00:07:24.164 --> 00:07:26.146
What are you talking about, Mother?

00:07:26.206 --> 00:07:27.987
It was a terrible line.

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:30.659
All I could hear was the sound of cars.

00:07:30.719 --> 00:07:33.362
I think he was phoning with his mobile.

00:07:33.422 --> 00:07:34.492
His what?

00:07:34.552 --> 00:07:36.044
It's, er...

00:07:36.104 --> 00:07:37.975
Oh, it doesn't matter.

00:07:38.035 --> 00:07:41.096
I want to know why he's coming home.

00:07:41.155 --> 00:07:43.566
It's only two o'clock in the afternoon.

00:07:43.586 --> 00:07:46.696
I told you today was going to be a bad day.

00:07:46.756 --> 00:07:48.607
I can feel it in my bones.

00:07:48.647 --> 00:07:50.027
Speak, Wyatt, Mum.

00:07:50.087 --> 00:07:52.548
I wonder what happened at work.

00:07:52.607 --> 00:07:55.158
It must be serious, don't worry.

00:07:55.218 --> 00:07:57.558
He just forgot something, I think.

00:07:57.618 --> 00:07:59.459
Yes, you're right.

00:07:59.519 --> 00:08:00.629
Okay.

00:08:00.689 --> 00:08:02.649
I can't sit around anymore.

00:08:02.709 --> 00:08:06.130
I can make Josephine's bed and tidy her room.

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:09.317
Thanks, Mum.

00:08:09.377 --> 00:08:13.796
Can you change the sheets, please?

00:08:13.856 --> 00:08:17.188
Yes, Nancy.

00:08:17.248 --> 00:08:24.413
Now, where are you, little thing?

00:08:24.473 --> 00:08:26.755
Oh, there you are.

00:08:26.775 --> 00:08:30.178
Oh, you're so sweet and cute.

00:08:30.237 --> 00:08:31.378
Come here.

00:08:31.398 --> 00:08:35.761
Oh, it tickles.

00:08:35.821 --> 00:08:39.144
Stop, Boris.

00:08:39.204 --> 00:08:40.905
Here, Robbie.

00:08:40.965 --> 00:08:42.026
Don't be afraid!

00:08:42.046 --> 00:08:43.988
That was not a mom!

00:08:44.048 --> 00:08:44.999
Nothing!

00:08:45.059 --> 00:08:46.570
Nothing!

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:47.231
Oh!

00:08:47.271 --> 00:08:48.682
Don't do that!

00:08:48.742 --> 00:08:50.424
Come out!

00:08:50.484 --> 00:08:50.914
Oh!

00:08:50.974 --> 00:08:51.455
Oh!

00:08:51.515 --> 00:08:51.775
Oh!

00:08:51.815 --> 00:08:52.456
That tickles!

00:08:52.476 --> 00:08:53.898
How are you?

00:08:53.958 --> 00:08:54.588
Oh!

00:08:54.648 --> 00:08:55.619
That was my jump!

00:08:55.639 --> 00:08:55.699
Oh!

00:08:55.739 --> 00:08:55.899
No!

00:08:55.919 --> 00:08:58.061
Stop that!

00:08:58.121 --> 00:09:01.664
What's happening in here?

00:09:01.684 --> 00:09:05.177
No, stop that!

00:09:05.237 --> 00:09:06.869
Oh, get off Boris!

00:09:06.929 --> 00:09:08.370
What's wrong?

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:11.312
Matt, what's the matter with everyone in this house?

00:09:11.352 --> 00:09:13.414
Who are you talking to, Mum?

00:09:13.474 --> 00:09:15.516
Oh, that tickle's stopping.

00:09:15.576 --> 00:09:16.887
What's happening?

00:09:16.947 --> 00:09:18.898
I'm home, what's the noise?

00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:22.872
Oh, hello Pete, I'm coming!

00:09:22.932 --> 00:09:25.174
Is that your mother?

00:09:25.234 --> 00:09:26.264
Yes.

00:09:26.324 --> 00:09:28.087
I don't know what she's doing.

00:09:28.147 --> 00:09:30.719
Maybe she had sherry on her cornflakes.

00:09:30.778 --> 00:09:35.350
She's Josephine's room, laughing her head off and I don't know why.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:38.250
Boris is sitting looking at her.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:40.941
She's getting old Nancy.

00:09:41.001 --> 00:09:44.331
Maybe we should start looking for an old fossil's home for her.

00:09:44.351 --> 00:09:47.062
Don't start that again, you know I get angry.

00:09:47.122 --> 00:09:53.353
Mum is staying with us and they are called old people's homes, not old fossils homes.

00:09:53.373 --> 00:09:55.174
Well I think we seriously...

00:09:55.194 --> 00:09:57.350
We can talk about this another time.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:59.317
Why are you home so early?

00:09:59.377 --> 00:10:01.068
You've never come home at this time.

00:10:01.088 --> 00:10:03.050
Oh, yes.

00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:05.942
Look, can we go into the kitchen?

00:10:06.002 --> 00:10:11.995
I can't concentrate with a laughing hyena upstairs.

00:10:12.055 --> 00:10:16.748
Sit down, dear.

00:10:16.808 --> 00:10:18.890
Would you like a cup of tea?

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:21.301
Something stronger might be a better idea.

00:10:21.361 --> 00:10:22.396
Why?

00:10:22.456 --> 00:10:24.081
What happened this morning?

00:10:24.141 --> 00:10:25.551
Tell me, please.

00:10:25.611 --> 00:10:27.142
I lost my job.

00:10:27.202 --> 00:10:28.282
What?

00:10:28.342 --> 00:10:29.173
Yes.

00:10:29.233 --> 00:10:30.454
I lost my job.

00:10:30.514 --> 00:10:32.715
I am now unemployed.

00:10:32.775 --> 00:10:35.106
Six of us from the office got the sack.

00:10:35.166 --> 00:10:40.152
We can work until the end of the month, and then thank you, but goodbye.

00:10:40.212 --> 00:10:43.098
I don't understand.

00:10:43.158 --> 00:10:47.782
Oh, that's what you were trying to tell mum on the phone.

00:10:47.842 --> 00:10:50.765
She thought you said you forgot the bag.

00:10:50.825 --> 00:10:53.147
She's deaf as well as losing her marbles.

00:10:53.207 --> 00:10:55.779
Okay, okay.

00:10:55.839 --> 00:11:01.844
Well, as I was saying, the company needs to save money and my department is being closed.

00:11:01.904 --> 00:11:03.586
What are we going to do?

00:11:03.606 --> 00:11:05.764
I can find another job.

00:11:05.824 --> 00:11:06.872
I hope.

00:11:06.932 --> 00:11:09.003
I think we must move house though.

00:11:09.063 --> 00:11:11.825
This one is too big and too expensive.

00:11:11.885 --> 00:11:13.346
We must save money.

00:11:13.406 --> 00:11:14.607
Wait a minute.

00:11:14.667 --> 00:11:16.188
I need to think.

00:11:16.248 --> 00:11:20.512
Be quiet mother!

00:11:20.572 --> 00:11:27.038
I'm just going to shut my mother up.

00:11:27.098 --> 00:11:33.894
What is the matter with you?

00:11:33.954 --> 00:11:36.344
Calm down, please.

00:11:36.404 --> 00:11:37.255
Stop it.

00:11:37.315 --> 00:11:39.866
Calm down and come downstairs.

00:11:39.926 --> 00:11:42.226
Pete has lost his job.

00:11:42.286 --> 00:11:43.146
Oh no.

00:11:43.166 --> 00:11:45.387
I knew today it was a bad day.

00:11:45.427 --> 00:11:46.787
Why are you laughing?

00:11:46.807 --> 00:11:48.408
I'm not laughing.

00:11:48.428 --> 00:11:49.558
Yes you are.

00:11:49.618 --> 00:11:50.948
No, I'm not.

00:11:51.008 --> 00:11:52.489
It's terrible.

00:11:52.509 --> 00:11:54.830
No, this is impossible.

00:11:54.890 --> 00:12:03.199
Stay there.

00:12:03.259 --> 00:12:11.980
Here you are Boris.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:16.674
It might be the last time you have meat for your dinner.

00:12:16.734 --> 00:12:20.188
What are we going to do Boris?

00:12:20.248 --> 00:12:23.921
I wonder what we're going to do.

00:12:23.981 --> 00:12:27.544
I'm hungry.

00:12:27.604 --> 00:12:31.735
Oh, school is bloody boring.

00:12:31.795 --> 00:12:33.535
Teachers are so dumb.

00:12:33.595 --> 00:12:35.176
I don't know anything.

00:12:35.236 --> 00:12:36.266
I'm starving.

00:12:36.286 --> 00:12:37.036
I want some crisps.

00:12:37.096 --> 00:12:40.027
If you wait five minutes, Josie, you can have something cooked.

00:12:40.087 --> 00:12:41.288
I'm making a curry.

00:12:41.348 --> 00:12:43.788
No, crisps are great.

00:12:43.848 --> 00:12:46.690
I want to find Julia.

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:49.300
She was at school all day today with you.

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:50.380
Can't she wait?

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:51.691
I want to talk to you.

00:12:51.711 --> 00:12:52.331
See ya.

00:12:52.391 --> 00:12:53.311
But Joe?

00:12:53.331 --> 00:12:58.484
It's easier to have a conversation with you, Boris.

00:12:58.544 --> 00:13:00.026
Boris?

00:13:00.086 --> 00:13:01.016
Boris?

00:13:01.036 --> 00:13:04.427
Come back, Boris!

00:13:04.487 --> 00:13:06.798
When is dinner?

00:13:06.858 --> 00:13:08.108
In five minutes.

00:13:08.168 --> 00:13:10.828
Okay, I just need to finish some repairs on the car.

00:13:10.888 --> 00:13:11.919
That can wait.

00:13:11.979 --> 00:13:14.539
There are more important things to talk about.

00:13:14.599 --> 00:13:15.890
Like what?

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:18.650
What planet do you live on, Pete?

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:22.071
At the end of the month, you have no job.

00:13:22.131 --> 00:13:23.841
Oh, yes, I forgot.

00:13:23.881 --> 00:13:24.751
You forgot?

00:13:24.811 --> 00:13:26.942
Don't you think we need to talk about it?

00:13:27.002 --> 00:13:28.984
I suppose so.

00:13:29.044 --> 00:13:31.695
Where do we move to?

00:13:31.756 --> 00:13:34.456
What do we say to Josie and Mum?

00:13:34.516 --> 00:13:36.987
I went to the estate agent some way home.

00:13:37.047 --> 00:13:42.329
I've got some information about a really nice two bedroom flat in Cedar Road near the park.

00:13:42.389 --> 00:13:44.259
Why didn't you ask me to come?

00:13:44.319 --> 00:13:45.959
I am your wife, you know.

00:13:46.019 --> 00:13:49.189
When we sell the house, we can easily buy this flat.

00:13:49.249 --> 00:13:51.840
It's got a nice balcony and a small garden.

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:54.971
You know you are always saying that the garden here is too big.

00:13:55.031 --> 00:13:56.502
There's too much cleaning and...

00:13:56.562 --> 00:13:58.522
Yes, yes, I know.

00:13:58.582 --> 00:14:00.343
We can go and look at the flat this evening.

00:14:00.403 --> 00:14:01.583
Okay.

00:14:01.643 --> 00:14:03.364
Wait a minute.

00:14:03.424 --> 00:14:06.245
How many bedrooms did you say the flat has?

00:14:06.305 --> 00:14:07.055
Back in a minute.

00:14:07.075 --> 00:14:09.506
Do something in the garage.

00:14:09.566 --> 00:14:12.287
Did you say two bedrooms?

00:14:12.347 --> 00:14:13.817
But...

00:14:13.837 --> 00:14:16.638
Where does my mother's leave?

00:14:16.698 --> 00:14:20.068
I feel a little strange.

00:14:20.128 --> 00:14:22.979
My muscles ache from so much laughers.

00:14:22.999 --> 00:14:25.449
Still don't understand why you were laughing.

00:14:25.509 --> 00:14:28.500
I think I need a little sherry to calm my nerves.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:29.960
Back in a minute.

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:31.481
What a house.

00:14:31.541 --> 00:14:33.411
It's like a railway station.

00:14:33.471 --> 00:14:34.782
I'm still hungry.

00:14:34.802 --> 00:14:35.922
I want some biscuits.

00:14:35.942 --> 00:14:37.723
Just sit down, Josephine.

00:14:37.743 --> 00:14:39.993
You can have some biscuits in a minute.

00:14:40.053 --> 00:14:41.584
Pete!

00:14:41.644 --> 00:14:42.774
Mum!

00:14:42.834 --> 00:14:44.914
Come in the kitchen!

00:14:44.974 --> 00:14:47.531
Now!

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:50.567
I said no!

00:14:50.627 --> 00:14:52.428
Keep your hair on mum.

00:14:52.488 --> 00:14:53.379
Chill out.

00:14:53.439 --> 00:14:56.151
How can I chill out when your father's lost his job today?

00:14:56.211 --> 00:14:56.672
What?

00:14:56.732 --> 00:14:58.473
Yes, you heard me.

00:14:58.533 --> 00:15:01.365
We have to move soon, find a smaller house.

00:15:01.425 --> 00:15:02.506
I want my own room.

00:15:02.546 --> 00:15:03.666
Yes, of course.

00:15:03.726 --> 00:15:05.828
I'm not sharing with anyone.

00:15:05.888 --> 00:15:07.670
Oh, that's better.

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:09.791
A little sherry always helps.

00:15:09.851 --> 00:15:12.413
Can you sit down please, mother?

00:15:12.473 --> 00:15:14.624
Perhaps you need a sherry too?

00:15:14.685 --> 00:15:16.398
No, I don't.

00:15:16.458 --> 00:15:18.201
What's the problem Nancy?

00:15:18.242 --> 00:15:21.897
Can we all sit down together?

00:15:21.957 --> 00:15:24.090
Good.

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:25.402
Right.

00:15:25.462 --> 00:15:26.983
Listen.

00:15:27.043 --> 00:15:30.914
In a few weeks, Pete has no job.

00:15:30.974 --> 00:15:33.074
We have to move.

00:15:33.134 --> 00:15:35.675
Oh, what a terrible day.

00:15:35.695 --> 00:15:38.255
And you bad things were going to happen.

00:15:38.275 --> 00:15:40.316
Be quiet, Mother, please.

00:15:40.376 --> 00:15:43.546
Yes, and I know the perfect place for us.

00:15:43.606 --> 00:15:45.717
It's in Cedar Road next to the park.

00:15:45.777 --> 00:15:49.338
I'm very close to your school, Josie, and the city centre.

00:15:49.398 --> 00:15:50.938
It's perfect.

00:15:50.998 --> 00:15:53.520
My friend Julia is just around the corner.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:54.270
Great!

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:56.852
Cedar Road is near the Bingo Club.

00:15:56.912 --> 00:15:58.283
I can walk there.

00:15:58.343 --> 00:16:00.174
I don't need to get a taxi.

00:16:00.234 --> 00:16:01.545
I don't like taxis.

00:16:01.585 --> 00:16:02.726
Tax is always smelly.

00:16:02.746 --> 00:16:04.217
Yes, okay mum.

00:16:04.277 --> 00:16:09.090
But the problem is that the flat peat found has only got...

00:16:09.131 --> 00:16:11.072
And Boris can walk in the park.

00:16:11.132 --> 00:16:14.853
As I was saying, the flat peat found for us.

00:16:14.913 --> 00:16:18.545
And it's only five minutes to walk to the shops.

00:16:18.605 --> 00:16:21.696
It only has two bedrooms!

00:16:21.756 --> 00:16:24.465
Oh, no.

00:16:24.525 --> 00:16:27.745
I don't want to go into an old people's home.

00:16:27.805 --> 00:16:29.626
They're full of old people.

00:16:29.686 --> 00:16:32.718
Don't worry mum, you don't have to go into a home.

00:16:32.778 --> 00:16:34.920
There isn't any other alternative.

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:36.090
Yes there is.

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:38.922
I'm sure we can find another solution.

00:16:38.983 --> 00:16:41.684
Sorry, but you're going to have to go into the home.

00:16:41.744 --> 00:16:42.715
That's life.

00:16:42.775 --> 00:16:44.346
It's alright.

00:16:44.406 --> 00:16:46.890
I know you don't want me here.

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:52.835
Last week, John, my friend Bingo, said I can go and live with him.

00:16:52.855 --> 00:16:57.590
He needs someone to help him, as he can't see very well.

00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:58.531
He's blind.

00:16:58.591 --> 00:17:00.036
Good thing too.

00:17:00.096 --> 00:17:02.772
Are you sure you want to do that, Mum?

00:17:02.832 --> 00:17:04.504
It's a great idea, Nancy.

00:17:04.564 --> 00:17:06.596
Yes, I'm very sure.

00:17:06.656 --> 00:17:09.700
You and Josie can visit me any time.

00:17:09.761 --> 00:17:11.232
It is nearby.

00:17:11.292 --> 00:17:12.203
There we are.

00:17:12.264 --> 00:17:13.926
Everyone is happy.

00:17:13.986 --> 00:17:15.878
Pass a biscuit, Josie.

00:17:15.938 --> 00:17:16.969
Thanks.

00:17:17.029 --> 00:17:19.777
Can't sit here doing nothing.

00:17:19.837 --> 00:17:23.094
Daddy's horrible to you, Gran.

00:17:23.153 --> 00:17:24.885
Why doesn't he like you?

00:17:24.945 --> 00:17:27.217
A good question, Josie.

00:17:27.277 --> 00:17:30.069
Does he like only one on the planet?

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:35.083
Only himself.

00:17:35.143 --> 00:17:41.198
Wake up, Pete.

00:17:41.258 --> 00:17:43.120
What?

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:46.458
Well, not now, Naomi.

00:17:46.518 --> 00:17:49.237
Oh, it's you, Nancy.

00:17:49.277 --> 00:17:50.858
Yes, it's Nancy.

00:17:50.898 --> 00:17:52.239
Your wife, remember?

00:17:52.299 --> 00:17:54.600
Yes, of course, Nancy.

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:56.582
Why did you wake me up?

00:17:56.642 --> 00:17:57.843
Because...

00:17:57.903 --> 00:17:59.594
Who's Naomi?

00:17:59.654 --> 00:18:00.925
Who?

00:18:00.985 --> 00:18:02.917
What do you mean, who's Naomi?

00:18:02.977 --> 00:18:06.119
You said, not now, Naomi, when I woke you up.

00:18:06.179 --> 00:18:07.130
I'm sure I didn't.

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:07.470
You did?

00:18:07.490 --> 00:18:09.981
Who did you think I was?

00:18:10.042 --> 00:18:13.564
I was dreaming of Naomi Campbell.

00:18:13.624 --> 00:18:14.845
Are you sure?

00:18:14.905 --> 00:18:18.406
If not, we can talk about this later.

00:18:18.466 --> 00:18:20.016
Come on, get out of bed.

00:18:20.076 --> 00:18:22.007
It's Saturday.

00:18:22.067 --> 00:18:23.657
I always get up late.

00:18:23.717 --> 00:18:26.318
Look, it's only half past nine.

00:18:26.338 --> 00:18:27.598
Don't argue.

00:18:27.658 --> 00:18:28.569
Get up.

00:18:28.629 --> 00:18:29.619
It's Mum.

00:18:29.679 --> 00:18:30.449
What?

00:18:30.509 --> 00:18:32.510
Did you pop a clogs in the night?

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:34.900
No, I'm pleased to say.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.681
Come on, hurry up.

00:18:36.741 --> 00:18:38.432
I'm going downstairs.

00:18:38.492 --> 00:18:40.372
They want all of us.

00:18:40.432 --> 00:18:41.873
What do you mean?

00:18:41.933 --> 00:18:44.247
They want all of us.

00:18:44.307 --> 00:18:47.402
I suppose I have to get up.

00:18:47.462 --> 00:18:49.693
Can you wait until tonight?

00:18:49.753 --> 00:18:51.994
Kneel me.

00:18:52.054 --> 00:18:55.355
I'm coming, I'm coming!

00:18:55.415 --> 00:19:00.357
Just waiting in the kitchen mum, Josie, Pete's on his way.

00:19:00.417 --> 00:19:02.638
This is so exciting!

00:19:02.698 --> 00:19:04.759
I think I need to go to the toilet.

00:19:04.779 --> 00:19:06.870
Do they want me in the photograph as well?

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:11.106
Yes, the whole family and Boris and Robbie.

00:19:11.166 --> 00:19:13.182
Robbie?

00:19:13.242 --> 00:19:16.038
Your father told you to sell that rat.

00:19:16.058 --> 00:19:18.634
Oh, well?

00:19:18.694 --> 00:19:20.327
No.

00:19:20.388 --> 00:19:22.999
I forgot to tell you, Mum.

00:19:23.059 --> 00:19:24.548
Don't worry.

00:19:24.568 --> 00:19:28.852
You know he's very quiet and clean and he can stay in my room.

00:19:28.912 --> 00:19:32.106
But I told you to- But he's house trained.

00:19:32.166 --> 00:19:33.558
He's so nice.

00:19:33.618 --> 00:19:34.538
Yes I know.

00:19:34.559 --> 00:19:38.042
He is quite sweet but what about your father?

00:19:38.062 --> 00:19:41.145
I'm sure you can think of something to say to him.

00:19:41.206 --> 00:19:43.548
Please don't tell him.

00:19:43.608 --> 00:19:46.171
I have to think of something to say to him.

00:19:46.231 --> 00:19:49.526
Children, what a life.

00:19:49.586 --> 00:19:51.540
Okay, just keep quiet.

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:52.954
Leave it to me.

00:19:53.014 --> 00:19:57.280
Thanks mum.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:04.386
What are the strange people in our living room on a Saturday morning?

00:20:04.446 --> 00:20:06.268
You still have your pajamas on?

00:20:06.328 --> 00:20:09.560
Yes, I didn't expect to find my house full of people.

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:10.530
What's happening?

00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:13.022
Oh, mega embarrassing.

00:20:13.042 --> 00:20:15.404
Why are you wearing those pajamas?

00:20:15.464 --> 00:20:16.314
I bought them.

00:20:16.374 --> 00:20:17.415
What's wrong with them?

00:20:17.475 --> 00:20:19.286
I like Winnie the Pooh.

00:20:19.346 --> 00:20:21.168
Tigger is my favorite.

00:20:21.228 --> 00:20:22.248
He's always so good.

00:20:22.288 --> 00:20:24.820
Can we all stop discussing my pajamas?

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:26.951
I wonder what thing about Tigger is.

00:20:26.992 --> 00:20:28.472
Be quiet.

00:20:28.532 --> 00:20:30.434
What's the matter with everyone this morning?

00:20:30.494 --> 00:20:32.375
Why are they sitting on our lounge?

00:20:32.435 --> 00:20:33.726
Because of mum.

00:20:33.786 --> 00:20:34.657
What did she do?

00:20:34.717 --> 00:20:36.658
Win the Nobel Prize for physics.

00:20:36.718 --> 00:20:38.229
No, Pete.

00:20:38.289 --> 00:20:41.151
She's our new special envoy at the United Nations.

00:20:41.211 --> 00:20:42.792
Don't we say nasty, Pete?

00:20:42.852 --> 00:20:43.864
No.

00:20:43.924 --> 00:20:46.545
Mum won a competition at Tesco's.

00:20:46.605 --> 00:20:48.336
A year supply of baked beans.

00:20:48.396 --> 00:20:50.428
No, something much more exciting.

00:20:50.448 --> 00:20:53.300
A lifetime supply of toilet paper.

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:54.751
No, Pete.

00:20:54.811 --> 00:20:57.533
Mum won a house.

00:20:57.593 --> 00:20:58.973
A house?

00:20:59.034 --> 00:21:00.985
A house?

00:21:01.045 --> 00:21:02.665
A what?

00:21:02.726 --> 00:21:04.457
For Boris?

00:21:04.517 --> 00:21:07.389
You do know what a house is, don't you?

00:21:07.449 --> 00:21:10.652
Of course I do, but I don't understand.

00:21:10.712 --> 00:21:14.235
Mum entered a competition at the supermarket last month.

00:21:14.295 --> 00:21:19.408
She had to guess how many jars of Marmite was sold in Britain every week.

00:21:19.468 --> 00:21:24.041
The prize for the nearest guess was a new detached house.

00:21:24.101 --> 00:21:25.552
She won it!

00:21:25.612 --> 00:21:26.993
I won it!

00:21:27.013 --> 00:21:28.184
I won it!

00:21:28.244 --> 00:21:35.838
I had no idea what the answer was, so I wrote down the first number that came into my head.

00:21:35.858 --> 00:21:36.868
63,360.

00:21:36.928 --> 00:21:40.460
I remember it from my primary school days.

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:42.041
Amazing!

00:21:42.101 --> 00:21:44.382
Absolutely amazing.

00:21:44.442 --> 00:21:46.974
Why 63,360 grand?

00:21:47.034 --> 00:21:50.486
It's the number of inches in a mile.

00:21:50.506 --> 00:21:52.637
Amazing.

00:21:52.697 --> 00:21:54.688
Absolutely amazing.

00:21:54.748 --> 00:21:56.269
Your cool grand.

00:21:56.329 --> 00:21:57.666
Awesome.

00:21:57.726 --> 00:21:59.574
And the people in our lounge?

00:21:59.634 --> 00:22:04.285
It's the local photographer from the newspaper and someone from the supermarket.

00:22:04.345 --> 00:22:08.066
They want to take our photo and give us the key to the house.

00:22:08.126 --> 00:22:10.177
Does this mean we can all live together?

00:22:10.237 --> 00:22:11.907
We don't have to move into a flat?

00:22:11.967 --> 00:22:13.788
Yes, that's right.

00:22:13.848 --> 00:22:16.808
Is that all right with you, Pete?

00:22:16.868 --> 00:22:19.599
Yes, I suppose so.

00:22:19.659 --> 00:22:20.399
Awesome.

00:22:20.459 --> 00:22:21.429
Come on, let's go.

00:22:21.489 --> 00:22:22.519
I'm coming.

00:22:22.580 --> 00:22:25.576
It is my hair all right, Josie.

00:22:25.636 --> 00:22:29.265
We're one big happy family again.

00:22:29.285 --> 00:22:34.238
I'm so happy we can go on living with your mother.

00:22:34.298 --> 00:22:37.120
We must be very grateful to her.

00:22:37.180 --> 00:22:45.470
That's the problem.

00:22:45.530 --> 00:22:54.420
It's a lovely house, Pete.

00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:56.611
Mum and I went to look at it this morning.

00:22:56.671 --> 00:22:59.764
It's ready and we can move in when we want.

00:22:59.824 --> 00:23:02.455
It's more modern than this house.

00:23:02.515 --> 00:23:05.217
The bathroom's a wonderful.

00:23:05.277 --> 00:23:06.938
The kitchen is wonderful.

00:23:06.998 --> 00:23:08.319
Everything is wonderful.

00:23:08.359 --> 00:23:10.140
The garden is wonderful.

00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:12.456
Yes, yes, I get the picture.

00:23:12.516 --> 00:23:14.602
Can you organise a removal firm?

00:23:14.662 --> 00:23:17.264
There are lots of advertisements in the yellow pages.

00:23:17.324 --> 00:23:17.994
Leave it to me.

00:23:18.014 --> 00:23:20.376
I have a friend at work who knows a firm.

00:23:20.436 --> 00:23:21.487
I hope they're good.

00:23:21.547 --> 00:23:22.628
Yes, yes.

00:23:22.688 --> 00:23:23.848
Don't worry.

00:23:23.908 --> 00:23:27.452
You are happy to move into this house with Mum, aren't you, Pete?

00:23:27.512 --> 00:23:28.432
Yes, dear.

00:23:28.492 --> 00:23:32.905
I mean, we have to move because of your job and this is the best alternative.

00:23:32.966 --> 00:23:34.526
Yes, dear.

00:23:34.586 --> 00:23:36.117
I know you're right.

00:23:36.178 --> 00:23:39.480
And this house is looking so shabby.

00:23:39.540 --> 00:23:41.022
What do you mean?

00:23:41.082 --> 00:23:44.274
Just look at this wallpaper here in the dining room.

00:23:44.334 --> 00:23:45.405
I like it.

00:23:45.465 --> 00:23:46.976
No, you don't.

00:23:47.036 --> 00:23:49.278
It's 23 years old.

00:23:49.338 --> 00:23:51.510
You just don't like doing DIY.

00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:53.502
I don't mind DIY.

00:23:53.522 --> 00:23:57.176
When was the last time you did anything in this house?

00:23:57.236 --> 00:24:00.298
See, I'm right.

00:24:00.358 --> 00:24:01.766
No, wait.

00:24:01.826 --> 00:24:04.384
I changed the light bulb in the kitchen last month.

00:24:04.444 --> 00:24:05.914
Need I say any more?

00:24:05.974 --> 00:24:08.235
Anyway, can we stop arguing?

00:24:08.295 --> 00:24:09.225
We're not arguing.

00:24:09.285 --> 00:24:09.925
Yes, we are.

00:24:09.985 --> 00:24:12.016
No, it's just stupid.

00:24:12.076 --> 00:24:13.086
I agree.

00:24:13.146 --> 00:24:14.236
Come on.

00:24:14.296 --> 00:24:17.327
We said we wanted to start the sorting out today.

00:24:17.387 --> 00:24:18.748
Okay.

00:24:18.808 --> 00:24:21.138
We can start with this cupboard of stuff.

00:24:21.198 --> 00:24:22.969
We never use any of it.

00:24:23.029 --> 00:24:24.509
Look, these for a start.

00:24:24.529 --> 00:24:26.300
No, don't throw them out.

00:24:26.360 --> 00:24:27.355
What about?

00:24:27.415 --> 00:24:29.324
They are old, we never use them.

00:24:29.344 --> 00:24:31.140
They might be useful one day.

00:24:31.200 --> 00:24:33.164
What use are six?

00:24:33.224 --> 00:24:35.329
Six, salt and pepper pots.

00:24:35.389 --> 00:24:37.970
Perhaps we have visitors in the new house.

00:24:38.030 --> 00:24:39.241
Visitors?

00:24:39.301 --> 00:24:41.032
How many are you expecting?

00:24:41.092 --> 00:24:44.884
The entire Hampshire cricket team and their wives and the crowd.

00:24:44.904 --> 00:24:47.125
There's no need to be like that, Pete.

00:24:47.185 --> 00:24:49.756
I just don't like to throw things away.

00:24:49.816 --> 00:24:52.958
But we said we were going to throw things out.

00:24:53.018 --> 00:24:56.049
We have too much stuff and we don't need it all in the new house.

00:24:56.109 --> 00:24:58.671
I know, but it's so difficult.

00:24:58.731 --> 00:25:01.422
What have we put in the box for the car boot sale?

00:25:01.482 --> 00:25:03.610
Let me look.

00:25:03.670 --> 00:25:06.330
A broken egg cup.

00:25:06.390 --> 00:25:08.532
Two tea towels from Mallorca.

00:25:08.552 --> 00:25:12.835
A frying pan with no handle and...

00:25:12.895 --> 00:25:13.446
Aah!

00:25:13.506 --> 00:25:15.327
Cuckoo clock with only one hand.

00:25:15.387 --> 00:25:18.390
Not very impressive for three hours work, is it?

00:25:18.450 --> 00:25:19.980
No, it isn't.

00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:21.252
Okay.

00:25:21.312 --> 00:25:23.904
We must try to be more ruthless.

00:25:23.964 --> 00:25:25.435
What do you mean we?

00:25:25.495 --> 00:25:26.986
Yes, I know.

00:25:27.046 --> 00:25:28.357
All right, Pete.

00:25:28.418 --> 00:25:29.518
Good.

00:25:29.578 --> 00:25:33.121
Now, what is this, a back of the cupboard?

00:25:33.181 --> 00:25:35.004
Give it to me.

00:25:35.064 --> 00:25:38.317
It's still in its original box.

00:25:38.378 --> 00:25:41.230
Well, it can't be important, surely.

00:25:41.290 --> 00:25:44.713
It's a pasta machine for making fresh pasta.

00:25:44.773 --> 00:25:48.506
You don't like pasta, so it can definitely go to the car boot sale.

00:25:48.526 --> 00:25:49.657
Oh, wait a minute, Pete.

00:25:49.717 --> 00:25:51.528
Now we don't need it.

00:25:51.588 --> 00:25:55.431
I just want to look at it for a moment.

00:25:55.491 --> 00:25:57.723
OK, now?

00:25:57.783 --> 00:25:58.954
Yes.

00:25:59.014 --> 00:26:00.065
You're right.

00:26:00.125 --> 00:26:01.498
We don't need it.

00:26:01.558 --> 00:26:03.662
Into the car boot box.

00:26:03.721 --> 00:26:04.322
Right.

00:26:04.382 --> 00:26:06.632
Might get £5 for that.

00:26:06.692 --> 00:26:09.684
You know it was a wedding present, Pete.

00:26:09.744 --> 00:26:10.644
Really?

00:26:10.704 --> 00:26:14.415
Another useless present, a complete waste of money.

00:26:14.475 --> 00:26:16.586
The things people buy.

00:26:16.646 --> 00:26:19.837
Why didn't we write a wedding list for everyone to choose from?

00:26:19.897 --> 00:26:22.878
Because you said it's more fun to see what people buy us.

00:26:22.938 --> 00:26:23.988
Did I?

00:26:24.048 --> 00:26:25.289
I don't remember.

00:26:25.349 --> 00:26:27.439
Anyway, into the car boot box.

00:26:27.499 --> 00:26:29.788
What a load of rubbish.

00:26:29.848 --> 00:26:32.977
You know that it was a present from your parents.

00:26:33.037 --> 00:26:34.528
What?

00:26:34.588 --> 00:26:36.099
The pasta machine.

00:26:36.159 --> 00:26:36.769
Are you sure?

00:26:36.829 --> 00:26:37.459
Yes.

00:26:37.519 --> 00:26:39.600
Look closely at the side of the box.

00:26:39.660 --> 00:26:41.391
You can see they wrote their names.

00:26:41.451 --> 00:26:43.062
Let me look.

00:26:43.122 --> 00:26:45.012
You're right.

00:26:45.072 --> 00:26:48.814
We can't throw this out, can we?

00:26:48.874 --> 00:26:50.615
Might be useful one day, Nancy.

00:26:50.675 --> 00:26:51.455
But you, sir.

00:26:51.475 --> 00:26:53.886
No, it's from my parents' dear.

00:26:53.946 --> 00:26:55.197
Right, what's next?

00:26:55.257 --> 00:26:58.120
What's in these drawers?

00:26:58.180 --> 00:27:00.101
Hmm.

00:27:00.161 --> 00:27:02.072
Interesting.

00:27:02.132 --> 00:27:05.403
I didn't know you were a member of Appa.

00:27:05.463 --> 00:27:06.824
Are you talking about...

00:27:06.884 --> 00:27:08.554
Oh, this photo.

00:27:08.614 --> 00:27:10.365
What are you wearing?

00:27:10.405 --> 00:27:12.146
It was questionable then.

00:27:12.206 --> 00:27:14.546
Everyone was wearing those skirts.

00:27:14.606 --> 00:27:16.057
What did you do with it?

00:27:16.117 --> 00:27:18.288
I would love to see you in it now.

00:27:18.348 --> 00:27:20.290
I think it's upstairs.

00:27:20.350 --> 00:27:21.932
Let me go and look.

00:27:21.992 --> 00:27:25.714
It's okay, I was only joking.

00:27:25.774 --> 00:27:28.696
What do you think Boris?

00:27:28.756 --> 00:27:30.528
Prepare yourself for a shock.

00:27:30.588 --> 00:27:32.299
Nancy in a mini skirt.

00:27:32.319 --> 00:27:36.282
I must try not to laugh too much.

00:27:36.342 --> 00:27:39.034
You keep quiet too Boris.

00:27:39.094 --> 00:27:40.846
Here she comes.

00:27:40.906 --> 00:27:44.805
Now remember Boris, don't start laughing.

00:27:44.865 --> 00:27:48.022
What do you think?

00:27:48.082 --> 00:27:52.634
I think it's shrunk in the wardrobe.

00:27:52.694 --> 00:27:54.436
Well?

00:27:54.496 --> 00:27:57.406
Well, say something.

00:27:57.426 --> 00:28:01.558
It's...

00:28:01.618 --> 00:28:04.379
So you think it's funny, do you?

00:28:04.439 --> 00:28:05.789
No, it's...

00:28:05.849 --> 00:28:07.640
It's...

00:28:07.700 --> 00:28:09.901
It's interesting, dear.

00:28:09.961 --> 00:28:11.571
Is that all you can say?

00:28:11.631 --> 00:28:12.932
No, no, no.

00:28:12.992 --> 00:28:18.494
Interesting and very interesting, dear.

00:28:18.554 --> 00:28:20.045
I've got to keep it on.

00:28:20.105 --> 00:28:22.556
It reminds me of Happy Days.

00:28:22.616 --> 00:28:25.718
Yes, you do that, dear.

00:28:25.738 --> 00:28:29.740
I need to go outside to wash the flowers.

00:28:29.800 --> 00:28:31.490
No, what's the car?

00:28:31.550 --> 00:28:33.001
No.

00:28:33.021 --> 00:28:37.203
Back in a minute, dear.

00:28:37.264 --> 00:28:43.397
We're moving at the weekend, Pete.

00:28:43.457 --> 00:28:45.328
Please come and help me.

00:28:45.388 --> 00:28:46.508
Where are you?

00:28:46.568 --> 00:28:48.229
I'm in the loft.

00:28:48.289 --> 00:28:51.170
There are so many boxes here.

00:28:51.230 --> 00:28:52.941
What's in them?

00:28:53.001 --> 00:28:54.392
Which boxes?

00:28:54.452 --> 00:28:56.153
Oh, those are my things.

00:28:56.213 --> 00:28:57.323
Don't throw them out.

00:28:57.383 --> 00:28:59.594
They're old things for my school days.

00:28:59.654 --> 00:29:01.215
I want to look at them.

00:29:01.275 --> 00:29:02.675
Oh, do we really have to?

00:29:02.695 --> 00:29:04.026
I want to look at them.

00:29:04.086 --> 00:29:06.897
See if you were a good pupil at school.

00:29:06.957 --> 00:29:07.848
OK.

00:29:07.908 --> 00:29:10.595
Here you are.

00:29:10.655 --> 00:29:14.153
Wow, sweet.

00:29:14.213 --> 00:29:17.335
It's your first writing book from primary school.

00:29:17.395 --> 00:29:18.875
It's embarrassing, Nancy.

00:29:18.915 --> 00:29:20.416
No, it's sweet.

00:29:20.476 --> 00:29:21.867
Look what you wrote.

00:29:21.927 --> 00:29:23.898
My name is Peter.

00:29:23.958 --> 00:29:25.248
I have a mother.

00:29:25.308 --> 00:29:26.489
She cooks.

00:29:26.549 --> 00:29:27.870
I have a father.

00:29:27.930 --> 00:29:29.780
He sleeps on the sofa.

00:29:29.840 --> 00:29:31.541
Do you want me like that?

00:29:31.561 --> 00:29:32.704
Yes, he did.

00:29:32.764 --> 00:29:33.847
and look here.

00:29:33.867 --> 00:29:36.698
There's a picture of you in a swimming costume.

00:29:36.758 --> 00:29:38.129
How sexy.

00:29:38.189 --> 00:29:40.030
No, I look terrible.

00:29:40.090 --> 00:29:43.601
I think that was the first time we went to Blackpool.

00:29:43.661 --> 00:29:46.062
I was six years old.

00:29:46.122 --> 00:29:47.442
What's this?

00:29:47.502 --> 00:29:49.163
I don't believe it.

00:29:49.223 --> 00:29:51.609
It's my old school uniform.

00:29:51.669 --> 00:29:53.265
What an awful colour.

00:29:53.325 --> 00:29:55.156
Did I really have to wear that to school?

00:29:55.216 --> 00:29:58.708
Oh, dark blue and pink stripes is very fashionable these days.

00:29:58.768 --> 00:30:00.329
Please, try it on.

00:30:00.389 --> 00:30:02.030
I want to see what it looks like.

00:30:02.090 --> 00:30:02.911
No, I'm not.

00:30:02.971 --> 00:30:03.691
It's too small.

00:30:03.711 --> 00:30:05.722
Oh, please, just for me.

00:30:05.782 --> 00:30:07.363
Come on, I can help you.

00:30:07.423 --> 00:30:08.034
I don't want to.

00:30:08.094 --> 00:30:09.234
Oh, don't be so stupid.

00:30:09.274 --> 00:30:09.965
Come on.

00:30:10.025 --> 00:30:10.575
No!

00:30:10.635 --> 00:30:12.016
Get off of that thing!

00:30:12.036 --> 00:30:15.054
Ah!

00:30:15.114 --> 00:30:18.554
Where am I?

00:30:18.614 --> 00:30:19.114
Oh!

00:30:19.174 --> 00:30:20.126
Oh no!

00:30:20.186 --> 00:30:22.419
There's a bird there in my room!

00:30:22.440 --> 00:30:26.186
He's coming through my ceiling!

00:30:26.246 --> 00:30:26.987
Oh!

00:30:27.027 --> 00:30:27.748
My leg!

00:30:27.808 --> 00:30:32.642
Go away, bird!

00:30:32.702 --> 00:30:37.113
Stop it!

00:30:37.173 --> 00:30:38.554
It's Pete!

00:30:38.614 --> 00:30:41.316
No worries, not dangerous!

00:30:41.376 --> 00:30:44.117
Just you, Pete.

00:30:44.177 --> 00:30:45.798
Is that you, Pete?

00:30:45.838 --> 00:30:46.868
Yes it is!

00:30:46.928 --> 00:30:48.249
Who else do you think it is?

00:30:48.309 --> 00:30:50.340
My foot hurts!

00:30:50.400 --> 00:30:53.382
Why is your foot through my ceiling?

00:30:53.442 --> 00:30:55.553
You know I have a weak heart.

00:30:55.613 --> 00:30:57.524
I almost died of fright!

00:30:57.584 --> 00:31:00.046
I always put my foot through the ceiling.

00:31:00.106 --> 00:31:02.217
It's a hobby of mine!

00:31:02.277 --> 00:31:03.318
What?

00:31:03.378 --> 00:31:04.758
What did you hit it with?

00:31:04.818 --> 00:31:06.740
I thought you were a burglar.

00:31:06.800 --> 00:31:09.111
I hit it with a bedside lamp.

00:31:09.171 --> 00:31:10.602
I think it's broken.

00:31:10.662 --> 00:31:12.213
I don't care about your lamp.

00:31:12.253 --> 00:31:13.934
I think my foot is broken.

00:31:13.994 --> 00:31:15.624
Help me, Nancy.

00:31:15.684 --> 00:31:17.656
Oh, be careful.

00:31:17.716 --> 00:31:19.146
Don't be stupid.

00:31:19.206 --> 00:31:20.537
You can stand up.

00:31:20.597 --> 00:31:21.488
Come on.

00:31:21.548 --> 00:31:22.939
I can't.

00:31:22.959 --> 00:31:24.720
You just want some sympathy.

00:31:24.780 --> 00:31:28.494
I can't stand up.

00:31:28.554 --> 00:31:32.548
Oh, perhaps you can't stand.

00:31:32.608 --> 00:31:34.549
Come on, Pete.

00:31:34.609 --> 00:31:36.369
Put your arm around my shoulder.

00:31:36.429 --> 00:31:38.299
Let me carry you to the bed.

00:31:38.359 --> 00:31:39.450
Oh, my God.

00:31:39.490 --> 00:31:40.580
Don't be so silly.

00:31:40.640 --> 00:31:42.150
Let me look.

00:31:42.210 --> 00:31:44.980
Oh, God, it's only sprained.

00:31:45.040 --> 00:31:47.141
There are lots of bruises.

00:31:47.201 --> 00:31:49.621
That's because your mother hit it with her lamp.

00:31:49.681 --> 00:31:51.022
She's very brave.

00:31:51.082 --> 00:31:51.982
Brave?

00:31:52.042 --> 00:31:53.732
She's dangerous.

00:31:53.792 --> 00:31:55.682
Send her away to any war zone.

00:31:55.742 --> 00:31:58.813
She could sort it out with this answer to Lambo.

00:31:58.873 --> 00:32:01.524
She is 72 years old.

00:32:01.584 --> 00:32:02.554
Hey, Rambo.

00:32:02.614 --> 00:32:04.055
How about a week in the Middle East?

00:32:04.075 --> 00:32:05.225
They need your help.

00:32:05.285 --> 00:32:07.226
I think you're suffering from shock.

00:32:07.286 --> 00:32:08.836
Here's some aspirin.

00:32:08.896 --> 00:32:10.706
Try to rest for a few hours.

00:32:10.766 --> 00:32:13.167
I can finish looking in the boxes in the attic.

00:32:13.227 --> 00:32:14.338
I can help.

00:32:14.398 --> 00:32:16.948
Oh, it's okay.

00:32:17.009 --> 00:32:28.964
I want to...

00:32:29.024 --> 00:32:39.930
The removal van is here.

00:32:39.950 --> 00:32:41.060
Okay.

00:32:41.120 --> 00:32:42.391
Is everything ready?

00:32:42.451 --> 00:32:43.391
Where's Pete?

00:32:43.451 --> 00:32:44.271
I'm ready.

00:32:44.291 --> 00:32:47.142
Oh, this is so exciting.

00:32:47.202 --> 00:32:49.992
Our new house and our new life.

00:32:50.052 --> 00:32:55.823
Where's Pete?

00:32:55.883 --> 00:33:01.254
Good morning.

00:33:01.314 --> 00:33:02.144
Come in.

00:33:02.204 --> 00:33:03.544
Good morning.

00:33:03.604 --> 00:33:04.625
Thank you.

00:33:04.685 --> 00:33:05.405
Come on, Jim.

00:33:05.465 --> 00:33:06.966
And we go.

00:33:07.026 --> 00:33:10.258
There are only two of you, is that enough?

00:33:10.318 --> 00:33:12.399
Jim and I always work together.

00:33:12.459 --> 00:33:14.060
No problem, madam.

00:33:14.120 --> 00:33:17.902
He may be over 65, but he can carry us over.

00:33:17.962 --> 00:33:19.663
No problem.

00:33:19.723 --> 00:33:22.104
Um, where do you want to start?

00:33:22.164 --> 00:33:25.056
Maybe a cup of tea before we start.

00:33:25.116 --> 00:33:28.201
It's a long day and we're both thirsty.

00:33:28.261 --> 00:33:31.146
Yes, I suppose that's alright.

00:33:31.206 --> 00:33:32.558
Come into the kitchen.

00:33:32.618 --> 00:33:35.640
Perhaps you have a packet of biscuits as well.

00:33:35.700 --> 00:33:39.744
A bit of toast and marmalade would be very nice.

00:33:39.804 --> 00:33:43.157
Sit down if you can find a chair.

00:33:43.217 --> 00:33:45.839
Everything is packed and ready for the move.

00:33:45.899 --> 00:33:48.793
We're okay, don't worry about us.

00:33:48.853 --> 00:33:50.405
My back.

00:33:50.465 --> 00:33:52.356
Bit of a problem with my back.

00:33:52.416 --> 00:33:53.716
But it's okay.

00:33:53.776 --> 00:33:55.196
No problem.

00:33:55.256 --> 00:33:56.957
No problem.

00:33:57.017 --> 00:33:59.437
I'm in the living room if you want me.

00:33:59.497 --> 00:34:00.708
Don't worry.

00:34:00.768 --> 00:34:03.288
We can start in a few minutes.

00:34:03.348 --> 00:34:05.139
Come here, doggy.

00:34:05.199 --> 00:34:10.424
Would you like a biscuit?

00:34:10.484 --> 00:34:15.141
Where's Pete?

00:34:15.201 --> 00:34:18.272
Why didn't you organise a proper removal company?

00:34:18.332 --> 00:34:21.084
The two of them are sitting in the kitchen eating breakfast.

00:34:21.144 --> 00:34:23.195
I think they were the cheapest.

00:34:23.255 --> 00:34:25.676
Why didn't I organise it myself?

00:34:25.736 --> 00:34:28.328
I can't get Pete to do anything.

00:34:28.388 --> 00:34:29.739
Where is he?

00:34:29.799 --> 00:34:31.079
Pete!

00:34:31.140 --> 00:34:32.820
Oh, let's go and find him.

00:34:32.860 --> 00:34:34.161
You stay here, mother.

00:34:34.221 --> 00:34:37.690
Okay, Nancy.

00:34:37.750 --> 00:34:40.901
There I am.

00:34:40.961 --> 00:34:42.443
What is happening?

00:34:42.504 --> 00:34:44.367
Good morning sir.

00:34:44.428 --> 00:34:45.450
Nice dog.

00:34:45.510 --> 00:34:47.043
Hello Pete.

00:34:47.103 --> 00:34:50.594
But why are you all sitting here eating?

00:34:50.654 --> 00:34:52.831
Don't feed Boris, please.

00:34:52.891 --> 00:34:54.302
I know, George.

00:34:54.363 --> 00:34:56.224
Is it my bingo club?

00:34:56.284 --> 00:34:59.646
We have a great time together, don't we, George?

00:34:59.706 --> 00:35:02.528
We certainly do, dear.

00:35:02.589 --> 00:35:05.071
Something happened to your leg, sir.

00:35:05.131 --> 00:35:06.452
It doesn't look good.

00:35:06.512 --> 00:35:07.542
Don't ask.

00:35:07.602 --> 00:35:09.634
But that's not important at the moment.

00:35:09.694 --> 00:35:13.407
I paid a lot of money to have you move us to our new house.

00:35:13.467 --> 00:35:16.758
I did not pay for you to eat our food.

00:35:16.818 --> 00:35:20.858
and stop giving Boris my favourite biscuits.

00:35:20.918 --> 00:35:23.109
I'm so unfriendly.

00:35:23.169 --> 00:35:24.789
I'm not unfriendly.

00:35:24.849 --> 00:35:27.620
I just want these men to start work.

00:35:27.680 --> 00:35:28.871
Okay.

00:35:28.931 --> 00:35:30.311
We understand.

00:35:30.331 --> 00:35:35.754
Come on, Jim.

00:35:35.814 --> 00:35:40.588
There you are.

00:35:40.648 --> 00:35:42.789
What did you say to the removal men?

00:35:42.849 --> 00:35:44.520
They look very unhappy.

00:35:44.580 --> 00:35:48.402
Typical workers sitting drinking tea and eating biscuits.

00:35:48.462 --> 00:35:50.653
I just told them to start work.

00:35:50.713 --> 00:35:52.494
He was very unfriendly.

00:35:52.554 --> 00:35:54.025
They are very nice men.

00:35:54.045 --> 00:35:56.926
Why do you always upset people?

00:35:56.986 --> 00:35:59.318
And why did you choose that company?

00:35:59.378 --> 00:36:00.608
They were the cheapest.

00:36:00.628 --> 00:36:02.419
I can see why they were the cheapest.

00:36:02.479 --> 00:36:04.440
Both of them look older than my mum.

00:36:04.500 --> 00:36:08.675
I'm sure they know what they are doing.

00:36:08.735 --> 00:36:11.690
What was that?

00:36:11.750 --> 00:36:14.002
I didn't hear anything.

00:36:14.062 --> 00:36:15.914
What are you doing now, Pete?

00:36:15.974 --> 00:36:19.838
Sitting and having a cup of tea and perhaps a couple of biscuits.

00:36:19.898 --> 00:36:21.159
If there are any left.

00:36:21.220 --> 00:36:23.082
I don't believe it.

00:36:23.142 --> 00:36:25.049
Come on, Mum.

00:36:25.109 --> 00:36:28.317
Sorry about the Vards, madam.

00:36:28.377 --> 00:36:31.509
My eyesight's not as good as it used to be.

00:36:31.569 --> 00:36:33.270
Got a bit of a shock.

00:36:33.330 --> 00:36:35.012
Thought I saw a rat.

00:36:35.052 --> 00:36:40.095
But I, uh, Josie, we don't have rats in this house.

00:36:40.155 --> 00:36:43.578
Don't worry, a bit of glue is all it needs.

00:36:43.598 --> 00:36:44.408
But it's just...

00:36:44.469 --> 00:36:48.902
But perhaps you and your mother could help us carry these boxes.

00:36:48.962 --> 00:36:51.944
They're a bit too heavy for the two of us.

00:36:52.004 --> 00:36:56.698
Yes, I always wanted to pick you up.

00:36:56.758 --> 00:36:59.031
You can pick me up any time, love.

00:36:59.091 --> 00:37:02.013
Come, Nancy, you stand in that corner.

00:37:02.033 --> 00:37:07.688
One, two, three, lift!

00:37:07.748 --> 00:37:14.762
Why did you choose that removal firm?

00:37:14.782 --> 00:37:17.465
Don't keep asking the same question.

00:37:17.485 --> 00:37:20.397
I know the answer, because they were the cheapest.

00:37:20.457 --> 00:37:22.289
Yes, they were the cheapest.

00:37:22.349 --> 00:37:24.450
How many more times do I have to tell you?

00:37:24.510 --> 00:37:25.972
But where are they?

00:37:26.032 --> 00:37:27.283
Be patient.

00:37:27.343 --> 00:37:28.604
Be patient.

00:37:28.664 --> 00:37:31.626
How long does it take to drive 15 miles?

00:37:31.687 --> 00:37:33.868
Well, well...

00:37:33.928 --> 00:37:35.491
Well, yes.

00:37:35.551 --> 00:37:38.063
Four hours is quite a long time.

00:37:38.123 --> 00:37:40.095
It's getting dark, Pete.

00:37:40.155 --> 00:37:41.646
See, it's getting dark.

00:37:41.706 --> 00:37:42.756
And cold.

00:37:42.817 --> 00:37:44.228
And I'm hungry.

00:37:44.288 --> 00:37:47.670
Yes, yes, and Boris is hungry too, I suppose.

00:37:47.730 --> 00:37:49.010
I know, I know.

00:37:49.070 --> 00:37:50.552
It's all my fault.

00:37:50.612 --> 00:37:53.313
We all make mistakes.

00:37:53.373 --> 00:37:56.365
Oh, here it comes.

00:37:56.425 --> 00:37:57.496
Ah, nah.

00:37:57.536 --> 00:37:58.447
You see?

00:37:58.507 --> 00:38:03.653
You see, everything is OK.

00:38:03.713 --> 00:38:16.495
you We're here.

00:38:16.515 --> 00:38:18.876
I told you, Jim.

00:38:18.936 --> 00:38:20.587
Sorry about that.

00:38:20.647 --> 00:38:21.978
We got lost.

00:38:22.038 --> 00:38:23.088
We got lost.

00:38:23.148 --> 00:38:24.828
It's only 15 miles.

00:38:24.888 --> 00:38:26.089
Yes, I know.

00:38:26.149 --> 00:38:31.951
But I wrote down Mulberry Avenue and Jim wrote down Mulberry Road.

00:38:32.011 --> 00:38:36.232
So, so first we went to Mulberry Road.

00:38:36.292 --> 00:38:37.213
But why?

00:38:37.273 --> 00:38:38.994
This is Mulberry Avenue.

00:38:39.054 --> 00:38:39.953
Yes.

00:38:40.014 --> 00:38:43.425
I know that now, but I didn't before.

00:38:43.485 --> 00:38:45.276
So where is Mulberry Road?

00:38:45.336 --> 00:38:46.286
I don't know.

00:38:46.346 --> 00:38:48.387
What do you mean you don't know?

00:38:48.447 --> 00:38:49.798
We didn't find it.

00:38:49.858 --> 00:38:53.100
There isn't a Mulberry Road, it's not on the map.

00:38:53.160 --> 00:38:56.212
So why did you look for Mulberry Road?

00:38:56.272 --> 00:38:59.663
Because Jim was sure that was where your house was.

00:38:59.724 --> 00:39:02.535
But where did you look if it's not on the map?

00:39:02.595 --> 00:39:03.686
Well, we...

00:39:03.746 --> 00:39:06.027
What happened to the roof of your van?

00:39:06.087 --> 00:39:07.368
Oh, yes.

00:39:07.428 --> 00:39:10.869
I thought you might ask about that.

00:39:10.929 --> 00:39:14.020
When we were looking for Mulberry Road...

00:39:14.080 --> 00:39:15.881
Which isn't on the map?

00:39:15.941 --> 00:39:18.882
Yes, which isn't on the map.

00:39:18.942 --> 00:39:24.844
When we were looking for Mulberry Road, we didn't see the low bridge.

00:39:24.904 --> 00:39:26.866
You hit the bridge.

00:39:26.926 --> 00:39:33.294
Yes, we hit the bridge, but only gently.

00:39:33.354 --> 00:39:36.063
Only Japanese.

00:39:36.123 --> 00:39:40.945
Don't worry, we can repair the van.

00:39:41.005 --> 00:39:43.417
I am not interested in your stupid van.

00:39:43.477 --> 00:39:45.028
What about our furniture?

00:39:45.088 --> 00:39:46.378
It's all a...

00:39:46.438 --> 00:39:48.399
Don't worry, no problem.

00:39:48.459 --> 00:39:50.944
It's just...

00:39:51.004 --> 00:39:56.661
There may be a few extra pieces of burning.

00:39:56.721 --> 00:39:58.232
What do you mean?

00:39:58.292 --> 00:40:10.363
Well, when we hit the bridge, gently, we heard one or two things move in the back of the van.

00:40:10.423 --> 00:40:16.989
So it is possible that one or two things are not exactly in the same number of pieces.

00:40:17.049 --> 00:40:19.541
I don't believe this is happening.

00:40:19.561 --> 00:40:23.044
Don't worry, a bit of glue is all we need.

00:40:23.104 --> 00:40:26.066
So you were telling us that our furniture is in pieces?

00:40:26.126 --> 00:40:28.217
No, I'm not saying that.

00:40:28.277 --> 00:40:29.869
So what are you saying?

00:40:29.929 --> 00:40:41.077
I'm saying that there is a possibility, only a possibility that your furniture is in more pieces now than when you bought it.

00:40:41.137 --> 00:40:42.028
What?

00:40:42.088 --> 00:40:43.618
Now listen.

00:40:43.678 --> 00:40:50.093
My family and I are going to leave you two here to move the furniture into the house.

00:40:50.153 --> 00:40:57.958
When we come back in three hours, we expect to find everything inside and you two waiting here.

00:40:58.018 --> 00:41:01.810
If everything is alright, you can have your money.

00:41:01.870 --> 00:41:03.471
Is that clear?

00:41:03.532 --> 00:41:05.883
Yes, but no problem.

00:41:05.943 --> 00:41:07.054
No problem.

00:41:07.074 --> 00:41:09.055
Can you stop saying no problem?

00:41:09.095 --> 00:41:09.936
No problem.

00:41:09.996 --> 00:41:10.936
Of course.

00:41:10.996 --> 00:41:13.092
No problem.

00:41:13.152 --> 00:41:15.198
Come on Pete!

00:41:15.258 --> 00:41:17.040
Get in the car everyone!

00:41:17.100 --> 00:41:19.762
Can you move your van so we can get out please?

00:41:19.822 --> 00:41:22.954
No problem, no problem!

00:41:22.994 --> 00:41:33.328
Get in the car Pete!

00:41:33.388 --> 00:41:42.730
Oh, what?

00:41:42.790 --> 00:41:48.583
They're not back with him!

00:41:48.603 --> 00:41:56.476
I can't!

00:41:56.536 --> 00:41:58.397
What's the matter with the door?

00:41:58.457 --> 00:41:59.067
Morning?

00:41:59.127 --> 00:42:01.378
Don't sit...

00:42:01.438 --> 00:42:02.418
My leg!

00:42:02.478 --> 00:42:03.419
What happened?

00:42:03.479 --> 00:42:06.810
I tried to tell you not to sit on that chair.

00:42:06.870 --> 00:42:07.890
Why not?

00:42:07.950 --> 00:42:09.384
What?

00:42:09.444 --> 00:42:12.460
Why has this chair only got three legs?

00:42:12.520 --> 00:42:15.062
I think you know why, Pete.

00:42:15.122 --> 00:42:17.464
Another piece of broken furniture.

00:42:17.524 --> 00:42:18.645
I told you.

00:42:18.705 --> 00:42:20.166
Oh, yes, don't.

00:42:20.226 --> 00:42:22.018
Don't.

00:42:22.078 --> 00:42:24.430
What is that noise?

00:42:24.490 --> 00:42:26.101
It's seven o'clock.

00:42:26.162 --> 00:42:27.743
Is someone cutting the grass?

00:42:27.803 --> 00:42:29.504
I think it's from next door.

00:42:29.564 --> 00:42:33.278
At this time in the morning, I'm going to tell them to stop.

00:42:33.338 --> 00:42:34.298
Be nice, dear.

00:42:34.358 --> 00:42:35.810
Don't be nasty.

00:42:35.870 --> 00:42:37.501
I am very polite.

00:42:37.561 --> 00:42:40.374
Leave it to me.

00:42:40.434 --> 00:42:43.775
Hey, Mad Max!

00:42:43.835 --> 00:42:46.456
Can you stop, please?

00:42:46.516 --> 00:42:52.677
Exterminator, can you stop, please?

00:42:52.737 --> 00:42:53.797
Yes?

00:42:53.857 --> 00:42:54.988
What's the problem?

00:42:55.048 --> 00:42:56.158
Good morning.

00:42:56.218 --> 00:42:57.658
My name's Pete Britton.

00:42:57.718 --> 00:42:58.878
We are your new neighbors.

00:42:58.938 --> 00:42:59.398
Hello?

00:42:59.458 --> 00:43:00.069
Good morning.

00:43:00.129 --> 00:43:01.109
Pleasure to meet you.

00:43:01.169 --> 00:43:02.789
My name is Derek Lump.

00:43:02.849 --> 00:43:04.520
Most people call me Colonel.

00:43:04.580 --> 00:43:06.050
This is the wife, Judith.

00:43:06.110 --> 00:43:07.346
Say hello.

00:43:07.406 --> 00:43:09.442
It's very early.

00:43:09.502 --> 00:43:12.114
Do you have to cut the grass at this time?

00:43:12.174 --> 00:43:14.505
Every morning, 0700 hours, precisely!

00:43:14.525 --> 00:43:16.415
100,000 men at 0600 hours.

00:43:16.475 --> 00:43:19.607
The wife gets breakfast at 0650 hours, don't you wife?

00:43:19.667 --> 00:43:20.907
Yes, dear.

00:43:20.927 --> 00:43:21.888
This is what?

00:43:21.928 --> 00:43:23.248
0645 hours, that's right wife?

00:43:23.308 --> 00:43:24.509
Yes, dear.

00:43:24.529 --> 00:43:27.160
Cut the grass at 0700 hours to 0730 hours.

00:43:27.220 --> 00:43:29.301
Then a long walk until 0900 hours.

00:43:29.361 --> 00:43:31.572
Got to keep fit, healthy body, healthy mind?

00:43:31.632 --> 00:43:32.362
Every day.

00:43:32.422 --> 00:43:32.892
Yes?

00:43:32.952 --> 00:43:36.634
Why don't you go for a walk first and then cut the grass?

00:43:36.694 --> 00:43:37.667
What?

00:43:37.727 --> 00:43:38.861
How do that?

00:43:38.921 --> 00:43:40.483
Who do you think you are tonight?

00:43:40.523 --> 00:43:41.504
Did you hear him, wife?

00:43:41.564 --> 00:43:42.424
Yes, dear.

00:43:42.484 --> 00:43:45.528
You cut the grass at this time every morning.

00:43:45.588 --> 00:43:50.183
This country is falling apart, typical of the younger generation, when I was younger.

00:43:50.243 --> 00:43:53.576
You cut the grass so early every morning.

00:43:53.636 --> 00:43:54.538
Yes, I can.

00:43:54.598 --> 00:43:56.560
I can do what I want in my own garden.

00:43:56.620 --> 00:43:58.942
No, you cut the grass.

00:43:59.002 --> 00:44:00.983
My name is Nancy Britton.

00:44:01.043 --> 00:44:02.573
I'm Pete's wife.

00:44:02.633 --> 00:44:03.574
Oh, Madam.

00:44:03.634 --> 00:44:04.824
Charm, I'm sure.

00:44:04.884 --> 00:44:06.084
My name is Derek Lump.

00:44:06.144 --> 00:44:07.395
Most people call me Colonel.

00:44:07.455 --> 00:44:08.505
This is the wife, Judith.

00:44:08.525 --> 00:44:09.116
Say hello.

00:44:09.176 --> 00:44:09.996
Hello.

00:44:10.056 --> 00:44:13.317
What's a lovely garden you have, Colonel?

00:44:13.377 --> 00:44:15.858
You must be very proud of it.

00:44:15.918 --> 00:44:16.598
Yes.

00:44:16.658 --> 00:44:18.138
We are, aren't we, wife?

00:44:18.198 --> 00:44:19.049
Yes, dear.

00:44:19.089 --> 00:44:21.009
It's very beautiful.

00:44:21.069 --> 00:44:24.180
I love the musical Windmill in the middle.

00:44:24.241 --> 00:44:27.011
And you have so many garden gnomes.

00:44:27.071 --> 00:44:28.532
They're very...

00:44:28.592 --> 00:44:30.343
Interesting.

00:44:30.403 --> 00:44:31.814
Please, you like them.

00:44:31.874 --> 00:44:34.225
We think they're very tasteful.

00:44:34.285 --> 00:44:36.997
And not everyone appreciates them, though.

00:44:37.057 --> 00:44:38.338
There are so many.

00:44:38.358 --> 00:44:39.138
274, to be precise.

00:44:39.158 --> 00:44:43.911
They are going to give you a guided tour of our garden one day.

00:44:43.971 --> 00:44:46.383
That would be lovely.

00:44:46.443 --> 00:44:48.004
Thank you, Colonel.

00:44:48.064 --> 00:44:54.618
But I just want to say how nice it is to have a wonderful and intelligent lady living next to us, isn't it, wife?

00:44:54.678 --> 00:44:56.088
Yes dear, I want.

00:44:56.108 --> 00:44:57.369
Too kind, Colonel.

00:44:57.429 --> 00:44:58.030
Thank you.

00:44:58.050 --> 00:45:17.079
Buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh-buh Why did you say all that?

00:45:17.099 --> 00:45:19.981
I was trying to get him to stop lawn mowing.

00:45:20.041 --> 00:45:21.141
Thanks for helping.

00:45:21.202 --> 00:45:23.904
All you can say is lovely garden.

00:45:23.964 --> 00:45:25.454
Lovely garden knows.

00:45:25.514 --> 00:45:27.786
They're absolutely revolting.

00:45:27.846 --> 00:45:29.367
I can't believe it.

00:45:29.407 --> 00:45:31.840
Of course they are revolting.

00:45:31.900 --> 00:45:35.544
I was trying to be nice to him, that's all.

00:45:35.604 --> 00:45:38.085
Your technique wasn't having much effect, was it?

00:45:38.146 --> 00:45:40.778
I think he was beginning to see my point of view.

00:45:40.838 --> 00:45:41.959
No he wasn't.

00:45:42.019 --> 00:45:44.030
You were shouting at each other.

00:45:44.091 --> 00:45:48.434
The way to deal with the Colonel is to use charm.

00:45:48.494 --> 00:45:50.906
Something you don't have much of, Pete.

00:45:50.966 --> 00:45:53.288
I can be charming if I want to be.

00:45:53.348 --> 00:45:54.643
You really think so?

00:45:54.703 --> 00:45:55.987
Anyway, come on.

00:45:56.047 --> 00:45:57.928
Let's do some more unpacking.

00:45:57.988 --> 00:46:00.489
I can't find anything I want at the moment.

00:46:00.549 --> 00:46:02.540
Why didn't you label the boxes?

00:46:02.560 --> 00:46:03.991
I thought that was your job.

00:46:04.051 --> 00:46:08.112
No, we agreed.

00:46:08.172 --> 00:46:12.784
Where is the kettle?

00:46:12.844 --> 00:46:15.365
Does anyone know where the kettle is?

00:46:15.425 --> 00:46:17.166
No, I don't.

00:46:17.226 --> 00:46:20.588
Where are my CDs of my MP3 player?

00:46:20.648 --> 00:46:22.178
I must have them.

00:46:22.238 --> 00:46:24.080
I can't live without them.

00:46:24.140 --> 00:46:25.491
No idea, Josie.

00:46:25.511 --> 00:46:27.253
Your mother was meant to label the box.

00:46:27.273 --> 00:46:29.364
Don't start that again.

00:46:29.424 --> 00:46:35.980
No, I don't know where your CDs and your ND tree player is, Josie.

00:46:36.040 --> 00:46:39.532
It's called an MP3 player, Mum.

00:46:39.592 --> 00:46:41.244
You're so stupid.

00:46:41.304 --> 00:46:42.615
Don't speak to your mother like that.

00:46:42.675 --> 00:46:45.267
We can look for it together if you want.

00:46:45.327 --> 00:46:46.826
Thanks, Gran.

00:46:46.886 --> 00:46:50.238
At least someone cares about me.

00:46:50.298 --> 00:46:52.760
This plug is dead.

00:46:52.821 --> 00:46:54.662
Nothing works in this house.

00:46:54.722 --> 00:46:59.156
The electricity doesn't work properly and the heating pipes make a very strange noise.

00:46:59.196 --> 00:47:00.898
The house is just new.

00:47:00.958 --> 00:47:03.571
It just needs a bit of love and affection.

00:47:03.631 --> 00:47:05.422
It's a disaster.

00:47:05.482 --> 00:47:08.268
But what happens when I switch on the fridge?

00:47:08.328 --> 00:47:10.151
The oven comes on.

00:47:10.171 --> 00:47:10.681
Yes.

00:47:10.741 --> 00:47:15.282
And when I switch on the kitchen light, the oven stops and the fridge starts.

00:47:15.342 --> 00:47:18.114
One or two wires across, that's all.

00:47:18.174 --> 00:47:19.874
It's rather fun, isn't it?

00:47:19.914 --> 00:47:21.265
I'm glad you think so.

00:47:21.325 --> 00:47:24.506
Try flushing the toilet while we look out into the garden.

00:47:24.566 --> 00:47:25.917
Are you serious?

00:47:25.977 --> 00:47:27.298
What do you mean?

00:47:27.358 --> 00:47:29.948
Just do, as I say, and watch.

00:47:30.009 --> 00:47:34.335
Oh, I want to do it.

00:47:34.395 --> 00:47:38.322
Oh look!

00:47:38.382 --> 00:47:40.645
How pretty the fountain is!

00:47:40.705 --> 00:47:43.790
It may be pretty, but it's not very practical.

00:47:43.850 --> 00:47:47.066
You need a workman to come and sort out the problems.

00:47:47.126 --> 00:47:48.808
On a Sunday, no chance.

00:47:48.868 --> 00:47:49.369
I know!

00:47:49.389 --> 00:47:52.406
And next door neighbour, we can ask him.

00:47:52.466 --> 00:47:53.898
Oh, no, Nancy.

00:47:53.958 --> 00:47:56.199
Please don't ask Lord Kitchener, please!

00:47:56.219 --> 00:47:57.380
He's offered.

00:47:57.440 --> 00:47:58.710
I can phone him.

00:47:58.770 --> 00:48:01.482
I even found the telephone directory this morning.

00:48:01.542 --> 00:48:03.933
Now, what was his name?

00:48:03.993 --> 00:48:05.754
Don't know lump.

00:48:05.814 --> 00:48:08.156
Direct lump, that's it.

00:48:08.216 --> 00:48:09.706
Here it is.

00:48:09.726 --> 00:48:11.667
465-9921.

00:48:11.727 --> 00:48:14.689
Give me the phone, Pete.

00:48:14.729 --> 00:48:16.370
Please don't, Nancy.

00:48:16.390 --> 00:48:21.904
465-9921.

00:48:21.964 --> 00:48:27.269
Hello?

00:48:27.329 --> 00:48:29.350
What hung out Chinese takeaway?

00:48:29.410 --> 00:48:30.890
What is your order please?

00:48:30.950 --> 00:48:33.260
Oh, I'm sorry, wrong number.

00:48:33.320 --> 00:48:34.520
Let's try again.

00:48:34.540 --> 00:48:40.512
4, 6, 5, 9, 9, 2, 1.

00:48:40.572 --> 00:48:43.332
Hello?

00:48:43.392 --> 00:48:45.412
What hung out Chinese takeaway?

00:48:45.472 --> 00:48:46.963
What is your order please?

00:48:47.023 --> 00:48:49.783
Oh no, wrong number again, I'm sorry.

00:48:49.843 --> 00:48:51.984
Very strange.

00:48:52.044 --> 00:48:54.100
The number is the right one.

00:48:54.160 --> 00:48:56.757
The telephone isn't working properly either.

00:48:56.817 --> 00:48:58.768
Unbelievable!

00:48:58.828 --> 00:49:01.270
Okay, you're right.

00:49:01.330 --> 00:49:04.693
Perhaps it's better to get in a professional firm in the morning.

00:49:04.753 --> 00:49:06.585
And I think there are mice in the house.

00:49:06.645 --> 00:49:07.406
What?

00:49:07.466 --> 00:49:08.666
I hope not.

00:49:08.726 --> 00:49:09.828
Look at my cardigan.

00:49:09.888 --> 00:49:10.775
Here.

00:49:10.836 --> 00:49:12.434
That's a hole, isn't it?

00:49:12.495 --> 00:49:13.856
It wasn't there yesterday.

00:49:13.916 --> 00:49:15.737
All your clothes have holes in them.

00:49:15.798 --> 00:49:18.400
I'm always telling you to buy some new clothes.

00:49:18.460 --> 00:49:22.174
Didn't an old lady give you ten pence last week when you were sitting waiting for the bus?

00:49:22.234 --> 00:49:23.416
She thought you were a tramp.

00:49:23.476 --> 00:49:24.466
Very funny.

00:49:24.526 --> 00:49:27.370
Look here, in this cupboard.

00:49:27.430 --> 00:49:30.572
And behind your chair, Nancy.

00:49:30.632 --> 00:49:32.084
Yes.

00:49:32.144 --> 00:49:34.547
They do look like mouse droppings.

00:49:34.607 --> 00:49:39.250
They're old and, erm, yes, they are very old and...

00:49:39.310 --> 00:49:42.052
So now you're both experts on mice, are you?

00:49:42.112 --> 00:49:44.544
You vacuumed here last night, didn't you, Nancy?

00:49:44.604 --> 00:49:45.534
Did I?

00:49:45.594 --> 00:49:47.266
I can't remember Pete.

00:49:47.326 --> 00:49:50.218
Maybe I did, and, erm, maybe I didn't.

00:49:50.278 --> 00:49:50.899
I saw you.

00:49:50.919 --> 00:49:51.980
Did you?

00:49:52.040 --> 00:49:53.160
Then I did.

00:49:53.220 --> 00:49:53.460
But...

00:49:53.480 --> 00:49:55.002
Maybe it's Boris.

00:49:55.062 --> 00:49:56.032
Boris.

00:49:56.092 --> 00:49:59.325
Boris, it can't be Boris, what rubbish?

00:49:59.385 --> 00:50:01.286
Maybe, erm, maybe it's...

00:50:01.346 --> 00:50:02.276
Yes?

00:50:02.336 --> 00:50:04.005
Maybe, er...

00:50:04.065 --> 00:50:05.553
It's you, Gran.

00:50:05.613 --> 00:50:07.464
You're all completely mad.

00:50:07.524 --> 00:50:09.445
Tomorrow, I'm going to buy a mousetrap.

00:50:09.465 --> 00:50:10.625
You can't do that!

00:50:10.685 --> 00:50:11.626
Why not?

00:50:11.666 --> 00:50:15.068
Because it might hurt him.

00:50:15.128 --> 00:50:16.969
It might hurt him.

00:50:17.029 --> 00:50:18.830
It might hurt him.

00:50:18.890 --> 00:50:20.180
That is the idea.

00:50:20.241 --> 00:50:22.082
It might hurt him a lot.

00:50:22.142 --> 00:50:23.932
And how do you already know it's the him?

00:50:23.992 --> 00:50:25.173
She doesn't.

00:50:25.233 --> 00:50:25.754
What?

00:50:25.814 --> 00:50:26.694
No, you don't.

00:50:26.754 --> 00:50:27.825
Yes, I do.

00:50:27.885 --> 00:50:28.795
What?

00:50:28.855 --> 00:50:32.054
You did sell that horrible rat, didn't you, Josie?

00:50:32.114 --> 00:50:35.581
Of course, uh, a little party on Saturday.

00:50:35.641 --> 00:50:36.712
Just the four of us.

00:50:36.772 --> 00:50:38.712
What are you talking about, Nancy?

00:50:38.772 --> 00:50:39.633
We're talking about...

00:50:39.653 --> 00:50:40.763
You thought fire, Nancy?

00:50:40.823 --> 00:50:41.954
Oh, you're right.

00:50:42.014 --> 00:50:43.384
It's November the fifth.

00:50:43.444 --> 00:50:44.635
Lovely idea.

00:50:44.695 --> 00:50:46.095
I can buy the firework.

00:50:46.135 --> 00:50:46.686
Cool.

00:50:46.746 --> 00:50:47.996
I want to do the music.

00:50:48.056 --> 00:50:50.447
Yes, Josie, but some nice music.

00:50:50.507 --> 00:50:51.838
All my music is nice.

00:50:51.878 --> 00:50:52.978
That's a matter of opinion.

00:50:53.038 --> 00:50:54.228
We can make a bonfire.

00:50:54.288 --> 00:50:56.059
Burn some of the rubbish in the garden.

00:50:56.079 --> 00:50:57.220
I like a good fire.

00:50:57.260 --> 00:50:58.144
That's my job.

00:50:58.204 --> 00:50:59.669
And I can do the food.

00:50:59.729 --> 00:51:04.243
Well, it's a good way to celebrate the first days in our new home.

00:51:04.303 --> 00:51:06.605
I hope everything works out alright.

00:51:06.665 --> 00:51:08.006
What do you mean?

00:51:08.066 --> 00:51:12.103
What can possibly go wrong?

00:51:12.163 --> 00:51:15.440
Come on, everyone.

00:51:15.500 --> 00:51:16.791
Let's go outside.

00:51:16.851 --> 00:51:17.922
It's dark now.

00:51:17.982 --> 00:51:20.324
Bring the sausages and the baked potatoes, Mum.

00:51:20.384 --> 00:51:22.236
Oh, it's so exciting.

00:51:22.296 --> 00:51:23.806
I'm coming.

00:51:23.866 --> 00:51:26.339
Turn on the patio lights, Pete.

00:51:26.399 --> 00:51:28.541
I think we can sit outside for a while.

00:51:28.601 --> 00:51:29.842
It's not too cold.

00:51:29.902 --> 00:51:30.692
OK.

00:51:30.752 --> 00:51:32.314
I'm going to stop the bum fire.

00:51:32.374 --> 00:51:35.406
Come and help me, Boris.

00:51:35.466 --> 00:51:38.033
Here comes the music.

00:51:38.093 --> 00:51:40.079
That's nice Josie.

00:51:40.119 --> 00:51:40.920
Well done.

00:51:40.980 --> 00:51:43.082
Where's the mulled wine Nancy?

00:51:43.142 --> 00:51:47.376
I think I would like a small glass on the table, but be careful mum.

00:51:47.436 --> 00:51:48.637
It's very strong.

00:51:48.697 --> 00:51:49.387
It's all right.

00:51:49.428 --> 00:52:13.669
That's it only one glass It tastes very nice maybe just another small one I don't think it's very alcoholic.

00:52:13.709 --> 00:52:16.091
Yes, Nancy, only one glass.

00:52:16.111 --> 00:52:17.892
Did you bring the sausages out, Mum?

00:52:17.952 --> 00:52:20.753
Yes, I put them on the table over there.

00:52:20.813 --> 00:52:22.164
They're not there now.

00:52:22.224 --> 00:52:23.344
Josie?

00:52:23.404 --> 00:52:24.736
No idea.

00:52:24.796 --> 00:52:26.636
I'm starving, where are they?

00:52:26.696 --> 00:52:28.648
Oh, no, look.

00:52:28.708 --> 00:52:31.359
There's half a sausage under the table.

00:52:31.419 --> 00:52:32.450
Boris?

00:52:32.510 --> 00:52:33.940
Where's Boris?

00:52:34.000 --> 00:52:35.551
He's over there with Dad.

00:52:35.611 --> 00:52:36.272
Pete?

00:52:36.332 --> 00:52:37.476
Come here.

00:52:37.536 --> 00:52:38.950
What's the matter?

00:52:39.010 --> 00:52:40.990
Look, the bonfire is burning well.

00:52:41.050 --> 00:52:43.541
Boris ate all the sausages.

00:52:43.601 --> 00:52:44.661
What can we do?

00:52:44.721 --> 00:52:46.132
I don't have any more.

00:52:46.192 --> 00:52:47.712
Bloody hell!

00:52:47.772 --> 00:52:49.822
No sausages, what a party.

00:52:49.882 --> 00:52:50.592
I know.

00:52:50.612 --> 00:52:52.933
Phone the colonel, his wife.

00:52:52.993 --> 00:52:55.183
Perhaps they can come over with some sausages.

00:52:55.243 --> 00:52:56.473
So I have to.

00:52:56.533 --> 00:52:59.204
Perhaps you can volunteer to be the guy for the bonfire.

00:52:59.264 --> 00:53:01.264
Just the podium, please.

00:53:01.324 --> 00:53:03.185
We are trying to be nice to him.

00:53:03.245 --> 00:53:10.771
Okay, okay.

00:53:10.831 --> 00:53:17.337
Hello?

00:53:17.397 --> 00:53:19.138
What hung out to any of us?

00:53:19.198 --> 00:53:20.709
Oh, it's your order, please.

00:53:20.769 --> 00:53:21.370
What?

00:53:21.430 --> 00:53:23.791
Oh, no, there's bloody phone.

00:53:23.851 --> 00:53:24.972
Still not fixed.

00:53:25.032 --> 00:53:26.632
And what is your order, please?

00:53:26.692 --> 00:53:27.393
What?

00:53:27.453 --> 00:53:28.974
No, I don't want the order.

00:53:29.034 --> 00:53:29.654
No.

00:53:29.714 --> 00:53:30.794
Wait a minute.

00:53:30.854 --> 00:53:32.706
Do you have any sausages?

00:53:32.766 --> 00:53:33.986
Slausages?

00:53:34.046 --> 00:53:35.527
What sausages?

00:53:35.587 --> 00:53:36.928
Don't you know what sausages?

00:53:36.988 --> 00:53:38.429
I mean, sausages are.

00:53:38.489 --> 00:53:39.870
No, please tell.

00:53:39.930 --> 00:53:42.101
Well, they are long...

00:53:42.161 --> 00:53:43.391
Oh, forget it.

00:53:43.452 --> 00:53:44.972
I can't be bothered to explain.

00:53:45.033 --> 00:53:46.442
Goodbye.

00:53:46.502 --> 00:53:48.160
What that country?

00:53:48.220 --> 00:53:49.931
Don't know what sausages are.

00:53:49.991 --> 00:53:51.262
Slosages.

00:53:51.322 --> 00:53:55.234
Unbelievable.

00:53:55.294 --> 00:53:59.746
Oh, I was trying to phone you.

00:53:59.806 --> 00:54:01.416
You don't have any slosages.

00:54:01.476 --> 00:54:03.157
I mean sausages with you.

00:54:03.217 --> 00:54:04.758
No, I suppose not.

00:54:04.818 --> 00:54:05.928
Sorry.

00:54:05.989 --> 00:54:07.769
Oh, hello, Colonel.

00:54:07.809 --> 00:54:09.120
Nice to see you again.

00:54:09.180 --> 00:54:10.760
Come in, please.

00:54:10.820 --> 00:54:13.312
Go and look after the fire, Pete.

00:54:13.372 --> 00:54:16.093
You're having a bonfire party, I see.

00:54:16.153 --> 00:54:17.683
Yes, we are.

00:54:17.743 --> 00:54:20.684
The wife and I were a little worried about your bonfire.

00:54:20.744 --> 00:54:21.164
Oh?

00:54:21.224 --> 00:54:23.725
Yes, it is very close to our fence.

00:54:23.785 --> 00:54:26.416
The wife and I were worried that it might catch fire.

00:54:26.476 --> 00:54:29.006
Don't worry, everything is under control.

00:54:29.066 --> 00:54:30.237
Where is your wife?

00:54:30.297 --> 00:54:30.997
She's not with you.

00:54:31.017 --> 00:54:34.608
No, no, she doesn't like to go out in the dark.

00:54:34.668 --> 00:54:36.778
Never know who you might meet.

00:54:36.838 --> 00:54:39.579
You didn't have a quick glass of mulled wine.

00:54:39.599 --> 00:54:42.540
Oh, that's very nice of you.

00:54:42.600 --> 00:54:43.976
Very nice.

00:54:44.036 --> 00:55:19.566
Ooh hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo hoo They dance well together!

00:55:19.626 --> 00:55:23.801
I hope Ren knows where she's leading him.

00:55:23.861 --> 00:55:25.271
What do you mean, Josie?

00:55:25.331 --> 00:55:25.992
Nothing.

00:55:26.052 --> 00:55:27.412
Nothing.

00:55:27.472 --> 00:55:28.222
Oh, no.

00:55:28.283 --> 00:55:29.453
Careful, Mum.

00:55:29.513 --> 00:55:30.703
Look behind you.

00:55:30.723 --> 00:55:33.724
What, as you say, I can't hear you.

00:55:33.744 --> 00:55:36.265
Leave it to me, Nancy.

00:55:36.285 --> 00:55:38.906
I was in the air.

00:55:38.946 --> 00:55:39.206
Help me.

00:55:39.246 --> 00:55:39.797
Help me.

00:55:39.857 --> 00:55:44.548
I'm too young to die.

00:55:44.609 --> 00:55:45.999
It's all right.

00:55:46.059 --> 00:55:47.860
I'm here.

00:55:47.920 --> 00:55:50.231
Oh, thank you.

00:55:50.291 --> 00:55:51.351
Oh, I'm rescued.

00:55:51.371 --> 00:55:52.662
Thank you.

00:55:52.722 --> 00:55:53.952
I'm all right, mother.

00:55:54.012 --> 00:55:55.443
Yes, Nancy.

00:55:55.503 --> 00:55:58.024
Just wet, let me cold.

00:55:58.084 --> 00:55:59.524
Come on upstairs.

00:55:59.584 --> 00:56:00.865
And you, Colonel.

00:56:00.925 --> 00:56:03.986
I can get you both some dry clothes.

00:56:04.046 --> 00:56:05.817
What happened, Josie?

00:56:05.877 --> 00:56:08.512
I didn't know your grandmother liked snorkeling in November.

00:56:08.572 --> 00:56:10.588
He looks like too much mulled wine.

00:56:10.648 --> 00:56:11.438
Oh, dear.

00:56:11.498 --> 00:56:12.479
What a pity.

00:56:12.539 --> 00:56:13.550
The Colonel as well.

00:56:13.570 --> 00:56:16.202
I hope they don't die of pneumonia.

00:56:16.262 --> 00:56:19.083
He'd be so nasty sometimes, Dad.

00:56:19.143 --> 00:56:20.834
It's just my sense of humour.

00:56:20.894 --> 00:56:24.566
Come on, hunt me with the fireworks for when the beached whales come downstairs.

00:56:24.626 --> 00:56:26.157
Just a moment, Dad.

00:56:26.217 --> 00:56:27.408
Back in a minute.

00:56:27.468 --> 00:56:31.500
Just want to get some one thing.

00:56:31.560 --> 00:56:33.682
Sorry?

00:56:33.742 --> 00:56:39.120
Sometimes I think I'm the only normal person in this family.

00:56:39.180 --> 00:56:43.326
Sorry, I am much better music, eh?

00:56:43.386 --> 00:56:45.336
You know your mother doesn't like it.

00:56:45.396 --> 00:56:46.946
Doesn't matter.

00:56:47.006 --> 00:56:48.587
I want to like a firework.

00:56:48.647 --> 00:56:49.797
I don't know about that.

00:56:49.857 --> 00:56:51.217
Oh, come on, Dad.

00:56:51.277 --> 00:56:52.468
Only one.

00:56:52.528 --> 00:56:54.218
I want to set off a rocket.

00:56:54.278 --> 00:56:55.908
OK, but be careful.

00:56:55.968 --> 00:56:57.078
No stress.

00:56:57.138 --> 00:57:00.279
Josie, what is looking out of your pocket?

00:57:00.339 --> 00:57:02.069
Is that...

00:57:02.130 --> 00:57:06.758
It's that rat.

00:57:06.818 --> 00:57:10.236
Give it to me!

00:57:10.296 --> 00:57:11.187
I told you!

00:57:11.247 --> 00:57:11.837
Stop it!

00:57:11.877 --> 00:57:12.717
Be careful!

00:57:12.777 --> 00:57:17.629
The rocket!

00:57:17.689 --> 00:57:19.189
What happened?

00:57:19.249 --> 00:57:20.730
Are you both all right?

00:57:20.790 --> 00:57:21.720
It's that rat!

00:57:21.780 --> 00:57:22.680
It's still alive!

00:57:22.740 --> 00:57:24.241
They're trying to kill Robbie!

00:57:24.301 --> 00:57:25.641
I told you to sell that rat!

00:57:25.701 --> 00:57:26.261
I hate it!

00:57:26.321 --> 00:57:27.302
It's vermin!

00:57:27.362 --> 00:57:28.402
I don't want to sell it!

00:57:28.422 --> 00:57:31.293
It's a strange smell of burning coming from somewhere!

00:57:31.353 --> 00:57:33.394
Are you cooking one of your casseroles, Nancy?

00:57:33.454 --> 00:57:35.123
No, I'm not!

00:57:35.183 --> 00:57:37.394
Where did the rocket go?

00:57:37.454 --> 00:57:39.207
I didn't see it in the sky.

00:57:39.227 --> 00:57:43.552
I think it was over the fence, it's an extra scar.

00:57:43.612 --> 00:57:46.106
No one was hurt.

00:57:46.166 --> 00:57:47.557
Look!

00:57:47.617 --> 00:57:48.938
Oh, no!

00:57:48.998 --> 00:57:49.908
My shed!

00:57:49.968 --> 00:57:51.479
My shed is on fire!

00:57:51.519 --> 00:57:51.929
Help!

00:57:51.989 --> 00:57:52.339
Help!

00:57:52.399 --> 00:57:54.910
Come on, help!

00:57:54.970 --> 00:57:57.802
What's a lovely bumper, Dexter?

00:57:57.862 --> 00:57:59.463
That's not a bonfire, Mum.

00:57:59.503 --> 00:58:01.003
It's a real fire.

00:58:01.063 --> 00:58:02.824
Phone the fire brigade, Pete.

00:58:02.884 --> 00:58:03.705
Come on, everyone!

00:58:03.745 --> 00:58:04.385
Get a bucket!

00:58:04.445 --> 00:58:05.445
Come with me!

00:58:05.505 --> 00:58:06.966
OK, where's the phone?

00:58:07.026 --> 00:58:08.226
It's absolutely typical.

00:58:08.286 --> 00:58:10.227
When he wants something, you can never find it.

00:58:10.287 --> 00:58:10.828
There it is.

00:58:10.888 --> 00:58:12.048
Behind you, on the bench.

00:58:12.108 --> 00:58:12.658
Oh, yes.

00:58:12.718 --> 00:58:13.789
Who put it there?

00:58:13.849 --> 00:58:17.164
Nine, nine, nine.

00:58:17.225 --> 00:58:20.980
Hello, what hung out Chinese?

00:58:21.040 --> 00:58:22.641
Not again!

00:58:22.701 --> 00:58:24.491
The Chinese take away again?

00:58:24.551 --> 00:58:25.672
Yes, what a day!

00:58:25.732 --> 00:58:26.662
What a day!

00:58:26.702 --> 00:58:28.973
This is a day to remember, I think.

00:58:29.033 --> 00:58:30.294
Yes, you're right.

00:58:30.354 --> 00:58:34.335
Still, there is one positive result.

00:58:34.396 --> 00:58:36.336
Please tell me what that is.

00:58:36.396 --> 00:58:38.687
I think the days are disaster.

00:58:38.747 --> 00:58:42.329
The lawnmower was in the shed.

00:58:42.389 --> 00:58:44.002
So?

00:58:44.062 --> 00:58:47.200
Oh, see, you were right!

00:58:47.260 --> 00:58:49.746
No more, more mowing early in the morning.

00:58:49.806 --> 00:58:51.511
For a few weeks, anyway.

